16
00:01:09,901 --> 00:01:11,835
- [Children Laughing]
- ' If I give the love you want you won't forget '

17
00:01:11,903 --> 00:01:14,804
' Girl, if I give the love
you want you won't forget '

18
00:01:14,873 --> 00:01:18,707
' Let this love light shine '

19
00:01:18,777 --> 00:01:22,144
' Let it in your soul '

20
00:01:24,249 --> 00:01:27,946
- [Kids Shouting, Chattering]
- ' Steady on forever '

21
00:01:28,019 --> 00:01:31,978
' It's time to take control '

22
00:01:32,057 --> 00:01:35,390
On your mark, get set, go!

23
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,861
' We don't need no darkness
We don't need no fear '

24
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:41,296
' We don't need no sadness '

25
00:01:41,366 --> 00:01:43,698
' It's already bright here '

26
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:45,498
[Cheering]

27
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:48,471
' Don't get upset
if you ain't got nobody '

28
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:52,943
' Don't get upset
if you have no fun '

29
00:01:53,011 --> 00:01:56,276
- ' Don't get angry '
- ' Don't get upset when you wake up '

30
00:01:56,348 --> 00:01:58,282
- ' In the morning '
- [Man] Hey, Derice, where you runnin', man?

31
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:00,318
- Yeah.
- Mornin'.

32
00:02:00,385 --> 00:02:03,183
- How are ya?
- '... new day life's just begun '

33
00:02:03,255 --> 00:02:05,655
' Ooo, yeah '

34
00:02:05,724 --> 00:02:07,851
' Give thanks and praises '

35
00:02:07,926 --> 00:02:09,917
- Hey, there.
- Derice.

36
00:02:09,995 --> 00:02:13,158
' Love is comin' your way '

37
00:02:22,174 --> 00:02:26,941
' Don't get upset
if you ain't got nobody '

38
00:02:27,012 --> 00:02:30,914
' Don't get upset
if you have no fun '

39
00:02:30,982 --> 00:02:32,916
' Don't get angry '

40
00:02:32,984 --> 00:02:36,545
' Don't get upset when
you wake up in the mornin' '

41
00:02:36,621 --> 00:02:41,684
' 'Cause every new day
life's just begun '

42
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,228
' Ooh, yeah '

43
00:02:44,296 --> 00:02:47,788
- [People Chattering]
- ' Give thanks and praises '

44
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:51,063
- Mornin'.
- Faster, Bannock, faster.

45
00:02:51,136 --> 00:02:53,400
Come on, child.
You have an Olympics to get to.

46
00:02:53,472 --> 00:02:57,238
Handsome as a lion, that one.

47
00:02:57,309 --> 00:03:02,076
I could watch that backside all day.
[Laughing]

48
00:03:02,147 --> 00:03:04,081
Come on!

49
00:03:08,286 --> 00:03:09,685
' If I give the love you want
you won't forget '

50
00:03:09,754 --> 00:03:12,518
' Girl, if I give the love
you want you won't forget '

51
00:03:12,591 --> 00:03:14,923
' Take away my sadness '

52
00:03:14,993 --> 00:03:17,359
' Take away my fears "

53
00:03:17,429 --> 00:03:20,830
[People Chattering]

54
00:03:24,336 --> 00:03:27,737
[Chattering Continues]

55
00:03:33,111 --> 00:03:38,674
Hey, Sanka, this
steering wheel is finished.

56
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:40,684
All right, team, let's get ready
for the pre-race cheer.

57
00:03:40,752 --> 00:03:44,244
- Ready? Ready?
- Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

58
00:03:44,322 --> 00:03:47,849
All right.
One, two, three, toot!

59
00:03:47,926 --> 00:03:52,226
[Chanting] Who's the captain of our crew?
Who's a friend to me and you?

60
00:03:52,297 --> 00:03:56,461
Kinda nice, good-lookin' too.
Sanka, Sanka! Yea, Sanka!

61
00:03:56,535 --> 00:04:00,096
[Laughs]
Get back to work.

62
00:04:00,171 --> 00:04:03,299
[Man] Who's the big, hot bag of air
who doesn't have to comb his hair?

63
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:07,175
Who doesn't bathe and doesn't care?
Sanka! Sanka!

64
00:04:07,245 --> 00:04:09,509
- Yea, Sanka! Hey!
- Sanka!

65
00:04:09,581 --> 00:04:11,419
What's happenin', star?
Where you been, man?

66
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:15,647
You almost missed my all-time,
world record seventh derby in a row.

67
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,854
Easy, Rasta.

68
00:04:16,922 --> 00:04:19,720
- I'm not gonna forget my best friend
on his day of days. - [Boy] Derice.

69
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:23,124
My grandfather says you're definitely
going to make it to the Olympics.

70
00:04:23,194 --> 00:04:26,163
He says you're even faster
than your father.

71
00:04:26,231 --> 00:04:29,564
- [Boy #2] Do it for Jamaica.
- You know what my grandfather says?

72
00:04:29,634 --> 00:04:31,864
- [Together] What?
- Get back to work!

73
00:04:31,937 --> 00:04:34,462
- Booie, booie!
- [Protesting]

74
00:04:34,539 --> 00:04:37,099
Good luck, man. I'll see you
at the finish line, all right?

75
00:04:40,412 --> 00:04:42,573
[Laughing]

76
00:04:42,647 --> 00:04:44,581
- Hi, Momma Coffie.
- Hi, Derice.

77
00:04:44,649 --> 00:04:47,846
- Derice, is Sanka ready?
- Who knows?

78
00:04:47,919 --> 00:04:52,686
That boy's never ready. He's a lazy,
crazy, sorry, no-good bag of bones.

79
00:04:52,757 --> 00:04:55,817
- [Laughing]
- So what you laughing at?

80
00:04:57,395 --> 00:05:00,057
All pushcarts
to the start position.

81
00:05:00,131 --> 00:05:02,827
- Ready, little man?
- Ready, big man.

82
00:05:02,901 --> 00:05:06,064
Kiss the lucky egg.

83
00:05:06,137 --> 00:05:09,436
- [Crowd Cheering, Shouting]
- Let's go.

84
00:05:09,507 --> 00:05:13,102
- On your marks.
- Feel the rhythm, feel the rhyme.

85
00:05:13,178 --> 00:05:15,703
Get on up,
it's pushcart time!

86
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:18,010
- And go!
- [Horn Blaring]

87
00:05:18,083 --> 00:05:20,745
Go!

88
00:05:22,587 --> 00:05:26,114
[Sanka] Here we go, Winston!
Me rocket has been launched!

89
00:05:26,191 --> 00:05:28,716
Hey, pokey!
Where'd you get that cart?

90
00:05:28,793 --> 00:05:33,423
Clear out! Move out!
Look out! [Laughs]

91
00:05:33,498 --> 00:05:35,932
Sanka Coffie!
Pushcart champion!

92
00:05:36,001 --> 00:05:39,061
- Pushcart champion!
- Get away! Get away!

93
00:05:39,137 --> 00:05:41,401
[Sanka]
Hey, grandma! Outta my way!

94
00:05:41,473 --> 00:05:46,274
Hey, Sunday driver! Make room
for the Rasta Rockett! Make room!

95
00:05:46,344 --> 00:05:49,609
- Sanka! Four more carts left.
- Pee wee, move! Move out!

96
00:05:49,681 --> 00:05:54,311
[Sanka] I love Jamaica
and Jamaica loves me!

97
00:05:54,386 --> 00:05:57,287
Champion! Champion!
You can't mess with the best!

98
00:05:57,355 --> 00:06:01,917
- Move over! Move over!
- [Winston] Get away! Get off me!

99
00:06:01,993 --> 00:06:03,585
- Come on, Sanka, get...
- Get him! Get him!

100
00:06:03,662 --> 00:06:07,098
One more time, Sanka.
Go, go, go!

101
00:06:07,165 --> 00:06:10,430
[Sanka]
Yes! We win! Oh! Oh, no!

102
00:06:10,502 --> 00:06:13,494
- No!
- [Screaming]

103
00:06:13,571 --> 00:06:16,506
Jump, Winston! Jump! Ohhh!

104
00:06:21,046 --> 00:06:24,311
Uhhh! Sanka!

105
00:06:24,382 --> 00:06:28,648
[Chicken Clucking]

106
00:06:31,856 --> 00:06:34,791
[Derice]
Move, man, move, move, move!

107
00:06:34,859 --> 00:06:37,657
Sanka. You dead?

108
00:06:37,729 --> 00:06:41,096
Yeah, man.
[Groans]

109
00:06:44,602 --> 00:06:47,093
And where do you think you're going?

110
00:06:47,172 --> 00:06:49,333
You caught me.
[Laughs]

111
00:06:49,407 --> 00:06:53,002
- You have papers to grade.
- I'm just getting in one last run.

112
00:06:53,078 --> 00:06:55,672
Mm-hmm.

113
00:06:55,747 --> 00:06:59,877
Can't believe the trials
are finally here.

114
00:06:59,951 --> 00:07:04,411
- You nervous?
- I'm not nervous. I'm ready.

115
00:07:04,489 --> 00:07:07,390
I've been ready for this day
my whole life.

116
00:07:07,459 --> 00:07:11,555
I don't care how fast they run.
I'm gonna run faster.

117
00:07:11,629 --> 00:07:14,462
I don't care
how much they want it.

118
00:07:14,532 --> 00:07:17,262
I want it more.

119
00:07:17,335 --> 00:07:20,361
I'm goin' to the Olympics, baby.

120
00:07:20,438 --> 00:07:23,999
I feel it.
I'm gonna win the gold.

121
00:07:24,075 --> 00:07:27,943
Derice, are you nervous?

122
00:07:28,012 --> 00:07:30,640
I'm terrified.
[Laughing]

123
00:07:35,887 --> 00:07:40,654
It's my turn, Joy.
It's my turn.

124
00:07:40,725 --> 00:07:44,058
[Man On P.A.] Ladies and gentlemen,
welcome to the final event...

125
00:07:44,129 --> 00:07:46,029
of today's Olympic tryouts.

126
00:07:47,098 --> 00:07:48,432
- [Crowd Chattering]

127
00:07:48,433 --> 00:07:51,899
- We have now come to the
main event of our games,

128
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:55,872
the running
of the 100-meter finals.

129
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:58,374
We've had a most
successful afternoon...

130
00:07:58,443 --> 00:08:00,877
and I'd like to congratulate
all of the athletes...

131
00:08:00,945 --> 00:08:04,244
who have participated
in today's events.

132
00:08:04,315 --> 00:08:08,115
- You sure no one can beat him?
- Oh, sure, I'm sure.

133
00:08:08,186 --> 00:08:10,279
I'm just a little concerned
about that big baldy.

134
00:08:10,355 --> 00:08:14,655
[Growling]

135
00:08:16,261 --> 00:08:19,162
Let me first congratulate our athletes
on a splendid performance.

136
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:23,064
And let me remind them that
only the top four finishers...

137
00:08:23,134 --> 00:08:25,295
will earn the right
to represent Jamaica...

138
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:28,965
in the forthcoming
summer games in Seoul, Korea.

139
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:33,306
- W-Wait. You're Derice Bannock, right?
- That's me.

140
00:08:33,378 --> 00:08:35,573
Oh. I hope I make the team.

141
00:08:35,647 --> 00:08:37,945
It would be a real honor
to run with you.

142
00:08:38,016 --> 00:08:40,041
- Good luck to you.
- Good luck to you.

143
00:08:40,118 --> 00:08:44,578
Derice Bannock.
Hey, good luck to you too.

144
00:08:47,859 --> 00:08:50,555
Runners, take your marks!

145
00:09:01,372 --> 00:09:03,567
Get set!

146
00:09:05,543 --> 00:09:07,602
[Starter's Pistol Fires]

147
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:09,943
[Crowd Cheering]

148
00:09:48,553 --> 00:09:51,681
[Derice] Mr. Coolidge, please.
You have to run the race over.

149
00:09:51,756 --> 00:09:54,281
[Coolidge] I'm sorry, Derice,
nothing can be done.

150
00:09:54,359 --> 00:09:56,293
But I was born
to compete in the Olympics.

151
00:09:56,361 --> 00:09:59,194
Then you're gonna have to work
on your boxing or your cycling.

152
00:09:59,264 --> 00:10:02,461
Those are the only other two sports
in which Jamaica competes.

153
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:05,093
I am not a boxer.
I am a runner.

154
00:10:05,169 --> 00:10:07,535
And it wasn't fair.

155
00:10:07,605 --> 00:10:11,200
It rarely is, my boy.
It rarely is.

156
00:10:14,646 --> 00:10:18,878
Well, Poppa, what do I do now?

157
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:23,512
Look, Derice.
Let it go, will you? Let it go.

158
00:10:23,588 --> 00:10:27,422
You will have
another chance in four years.

159
00:10:27,492 --> 00:10:31,326
Yeah.

160
00:10:31,396 --> 00:10:35,924
Mr. Coolidge, who's the other man
in the picture with my father?

161
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,560
Irving Blitzer.
He's an American who lives here.

162
00:10:38,636 --> 00:10:41,264
Unless, of course,
he's been arrested or shot.

163
00:10:41,339 --> 00:10:44,433
- Excuse me?
- Well, he's a bookie now.

164
00:10:44,509 --> 00:10:48,070
Takes his bets in a small pool hall
just past Sandy Bay.

165
00:10:48,146 --> 00:10:50,171
Isn't that a gold medal
around his neck?

166
00:10:50,248 --> 00:10:53,308
Oh, yeah. That lunatic
was an Olympic bobsledder...

167
00:10:53,384 --> 00:10:56,785
who tried to get your father
to switch sports.

168
00:10:56,854 --> 00:11:01,518
He had some theory about using
track sprinters to push the bobsled.

169
00:11:01,592 --> 00:11:04,857
Some ridiculous thing like that.
Can you imagine,

170
00:11:04,929 --> 00:11:07,796
a Jamaican bobsledder?

171
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,147
- And you sure this man,
he lives on the island?

172
00:11:12,148 --> 00:11:13,231
- Oh, yes.

173
00:11:13,304 --> 00:11:16,102
- Mr. Coolidge, thanks a lot.
- Good, Derice.

174
00:11:16,174 --> 00:11:19,735
- Oh. Could I borrow this picture?
- Bring it back.

175
00:11:19,811 --> 00:11:22,143
Yes. Thanks a lot,
Mr. Coolidge.

176
00:11:22,213 --> 00:11:24,909
- Oh. Just one more thing.
- Hmm?

177
00:11:24,983 --> 00:11:28,146
What's a bobsled?

178
00:11:29,687 --> 00:11:31,951
That's a bobsled!

179
00:11:32,023 --> 00:11:35,891
Oh! So a bobsled is
a pushcart with no wheels.

180
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:39,555
- That's what it looks like here.
- Let me see that.

181
00:11:43,401 --> 00:11:46,734
All right. "The key elements
for a successful sled team...

182
00:11:46,804 --> 00:11:51,298
are a steady driver and three strong
runners to push off down the ice."

183
00:11:51,376 --> 00:11:54,641
Ice! Ice!

184
00:11:54,712 --> 00:12:00,173
Well... it's kind of
a winter sport, you know.

185
00:12:00,251 --> 00:12:04,415
- You mean winter as in ice?
- Maybe.

186
00:12:04,489 --> 00:12:08,482
You mean winter as in igloos
and Eskimos and penguins and ice?

187
00:12:08,559 --> 00:12:11,960
- Possibly.
- See ya.

188
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:14,828
- Where you goin'?
- I'm gonna take a hot bath.

189
00:12:14,899 --> 00:12:17,026
I'm gettin' cold just thinkin'
about all this ice.

190
00:12:17,101 --> 00:12:19,661
No, man! You're gonna be
part of my bobsled team.

191
00:12:19,737 --> 00:12:21,671
What you need me for?

192
00:12:21,739 --> 00:12:24,572
Who... is the best
pushcart driver...

193
00:12:24,642 --> 00:12:27,406
- In all of Jamaica?
- You're lookin' at him!

194
00:12:27,478 --> 00:12:30,413
- Then you're gonna do it?
- No!

195
00:12:30,481 --> 00:12:32,642
Hey, man, you could be famous.

196
00:12:32,717 --> 00:12:36,312
You could have your picture
on a Wheaties box.

197
00:12:36,387 --> 00:12:40,187
But you said no, and that's all right
because I don't need ya.

198
00:12:40,258 --> 00:12:43,887
Everybody is gonna want to be
on my bobsled team.

199
00:12:43,961 --> 00:12:47,260
Look, star, let me tell you
a little somethin', all right?

200
00:12:47,331 --> 00:12:48,348
When you need something from me,

201
00:12:48,349 --> 00:12:50,789
you don't have to hand me a bunch of lines.

202
00:12:50,868 --> 00:12:52,802
All you have to do is
look at me in the eye and say,

203
00:12:52,803 --> 00:12:54,330
"Sanka, you are my best friend.

204
00:12:54,331 --> 00:12:58,634
We've been through a whole heap together
and I really, really need you."

205
00:13:00,978 --> 00:13:02,843
Sanka, you're right.

206
00:13:02,914 --> 00:13:04,667
And you are my best friend.

207
00:13:04,668 --> 00:13:06,372
And we've been through a whole lot together.

208
00:13:06,451 --> 00:13:10,251
- Heap. Heap.
- Sorry, man. A whole heap together.

209
00:13:10,321 --> 00:13:12,551
And I really, really need you.

210
00:13:12,623 --> 00:13:14,918
- And I really, really need you.

211
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:15,922
- Forget it!

212
00:13:15,993 --> 00:13:18,188
- But you just said if I said that, man...
- All right, all right,

213
00:13:18,262 --> 00:13:20,196
all right.

214
00:13:20,264 --> 00:13:22,198
All right, man.

215
00:13:22,266 --> 00:13:24,530
[Sanka] So, let's talk
about this "billsled" team.

216
00:13:24,602 --> 00:13:27,469
- [Derice] No. Bobsled team.
- Whoever.

217
00:13:27,538 --> 00:13:31,235
[Sanka] Now about the Wheaties box.
I'm gonna be on it by myself, right?

218
00:13:31,309 --> 00:13:33,573
No, man, you're gonna be
on it with me.

219
00:13:33,644 --> 00:13:35,976
[Man On Radio] And down the stretch
they come! Tumbleweed is holding on...

220
00:13:36,047 --> 00:13:38,413
- As Captain Video is still running on the outside.
- Yes, Tumbleweed, yes!

221
00:13:38,483 --> 00:13:40,951
...is dropping back as Tumbleweed holds the rail.
- Come on! That's it!

222
00:13:41,018 --> 00:13:43,248
Good Tumbleweed!
Good Tumbleweed!

223
00:13:43,321 --> 00:13:46,779
- Tumbleweed is slowing!
- No, Tumbleweed, no! Bad Tumbleweed!

224
00:13:46,858 --> 00:13:47,951
- What are you doin'?

225
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:50,316
- Tumbleweed can't hold it as
he gets pinned against the rail.

226
00:13:50,394 --> 00:13:53,989
Don't do that!
Let him out!

227
00:13:54,065 --> 00:13:56,090
- Don't! I need this one!  - Tumbleweed is
running gamely, but Captain Video...

228
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:58,101
- Seems just a little bit too strong.
- Please! Come on!

229
00:13:58,169 --> 00:14:00,296
- Here they come! Yes!
- No!

230
00:14:00,371 --> 00:14:02,635
Tumbleweed can't hold it
as Captain Video takes charge.

231
00:14:02,707 --> 00:14:06,074
- And it's Brewster finishing in second.
Susan's Pride... - What?

232
00:14:06,144 --> 00:14:08,510
finishes third and Tumbleweed
is nowhere in sight.

233
00:14:08,579 --> 00:14:11,295
But my, oh, my, the
odds-on favorite showed

234
00:14:11,296 --> 00:14:12,811
his true colors with
that late stretch run.

235
00:14:12,884 --> 00:14:15,717
- Uh-huh.  - Tumbleweed held on
momentarily, but realistically,

236
00:14:15,786 --> 00:14:18,448
only a fool would put
their money on Tumbleweed.

237
00:14:18,523 --> 00:14:22,323
- That horse had no chance whatsoev...
- Uh-huh! Uh-huh! Uh-huh!

238
00:14:22,393 --> 00:14:25,123
Uh-huh! Uh-huh!

239
00:14:25,196 --> 00:14:27,790
That guy won two gold medals?

240
00:14:30,301 --> 00:14:33,896
I think so.

241
00:14:33,971 --> 00:14:37,907
[Sighs]

242
00:14:37,975 --> 00:14:42,002
That's Tumbleweed gone.
Okay, next race.

243
00:14:45,449 --> 00:14:48,782
Excuse, me.
Are you Mr. Irving Blitzer?

244
00:14:48,853 --> 00:14:51,014
Well, that depends
on who's asking.

245
00:14:51,088 --> 00:14:54,888
My name is Derice Bannock.
This is my teammate, Sanka Coffie.

246
00:14:54,959 --> 00:14:57,120
Greetings, sled god.

247
00:14:57,195 --> 00:14:59,322
We were just wondering
if you'd be interested...

248
00:14:59,397 --> 00:15:03,527
in coaching the first
Jamaican bobsled team.

249
00:15:03,601 --> 00:15:06,866
Derice, remember the radio?
Radio?

250
00:15:06,938 --> 00:15:09,964
Stick. Shooting
with the stick. Let's go!

251
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:12,407
Let's go, Derice!

252
00:15:25,189 --> 00:15:27,521
Come on, coach.

253
00:15:27,592 --> 00:15:30,857
Just help me get started.

254
00:15:30,928 --> 00:15:32,896
[Derice Groans]

255
00:15:41,539 --> 00:15:43,530
- Oh!
- Greetings, sled god.

256
00:15:43,608 --> 00:15:47,704
- Sorry to bother you, but you're the
only one who can help us.  - Get out! Get out!

257
00:15:47,778 --> 00:15:51,714
[Sighs, Groans]

258
00:15:51,782 --> 00:15:53,716
[Toilet Flushing]

259
00:15:56,053 --> 00:15:59,318
- Go away.
- Okay.

260
00:15:59,390 --> 00:16:01,654
Nice to meet you!

261
00:16:01,726 --> 00:16:05,059
- Maybe today is a bad day.
- Yeah.

262
00:16:05,129 --> 00:16:10,032
I'll come back tomorrow.
And the next day. And the next day.

263
00:16:10,101 --> 00:16:13,537
- No! Look, whatever your name is...
- Derice.

264
00:16:13,604 --> 00:16:17,096
All right, Derice. Let me lay out
some difficulties for you.

265
00:16:17,174 --> 00:16:21,770
Snow. You don't have any.
It's 900 degrees out there.

266
00:16:21,846 --> 00:16:25,646
Time. You don't have any.
The Olympics are in three months.

267
00:16:25,716 --> 00:16:29,277
And me. You don't have me.

268
00:16:29,353 --> 00:16:32,754
As far as I'm concerned, the sport
of bobsledding no longer exists.

269
00:16:32,823 --> 00:16:35,348
I don't want to do it,
I don't want to coach it,

270
00:16:35,426 --> 00:16:38,691
and most of all,
and I mean most of all,

271
00:16:38,763 --> 00:16:43,029
I don't want to be within
2,000 miles of anyone who does.

272
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:45,034
Now, did you follow all that?

273
00:16:45,102 --> 00:16:47,662
Then how come you still have
that poster on the wall?

274
00:16:50,274 --> 00:16:53,607
Is that what's bothering you?

275
00:16:56,314 --> 00:17:00,717
There. Is that better?
Are you happy?

276
00:17:08,025 --> 00:17:12,052
Like I said...
my name is Derice Bannock.

277
00:17:12,129 --> 00:17:15,121
I'm Ben Bannock's son.

278
00:17:18,769 --> 00:17:22,227
I haven't seen this picture
in 20 years.

279
00:17:22,306 --> 00:17:26,333
Huh. Would you look at me then?

280
00:17:26,410 --> 00:17:29,345
Whoo. Would you look at me now.

281
00:17:29,413 --> 00:17:33,315
Please, Mr. Blitzer,
just give me a chance.

282
00:17:33,384 --> 00:17:36,649
If I don't have what it takes,
we'll forget the whole thing.

283
00:17:36,721 --> 00:17:39,246
Believe me, kid,
you do not have what it takes.

284
00:17:39,323 --> 00:17:42,121
- But you thought my father did.
- Your father was one of...

285
00:17:42,193 --> 00:17:45,526
the toughest competitors I ever saw.

286
00:17:45,596 --> 00:17:48,861
He ran the 100 meters in ten-flat.

287
00:17:48,933 --> 00:17:51,993
Well, I run it in nine-nine.

288
00:17:54,071 --> 00:17:58,132
Come on. Coach me.

289
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:03,476
Sorry.
You're a couple decades late.

290
00:18:03,547 --> 00:18:06,675
Oh, I see. It might be easy
for you to walk away from me,

291
00:18:06,751 --> 00:18:09,652
Mr. Blitzer, but you can't
walk away from this:

292
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,847
Twenty years ago
you came down here to see...

293
00:18:11,922 --> 00:18:15,016
if you could make a Jamaican sprinter
into a bobsledder,

294
00:18:15,092 --> 00:18:17,492
and you never got that chance.

295
00:18:17,561 --> 00:18:21,657
Look at me, Mr. Blitzer.
I'm your chance.

296
00:18:21,732 --> 00:18:23,825
Take it.

297
00:18:28,305 --> 00:18:30,239
[Exhaling]

298
00:18:30,408 --> 00:18:33,468
- [Crowd Chattering]
- " [Reggae]

299
00:18:34,945 --> 00:18:37,345
All right.
Everyone quiet down.

300
00:18:37,415 --> 00:18:41,317
Nice group here.
Now, for two of you lucky people,

301
00:18:41,385 --> 00:18:45,082
our trip to the Olympics
starts right now.

302
00:18:46,490 --> 00:18:50,790
And I want to introduce you...
to Mr. Irving Blitzer...

303
00:18:50,861 --> 00:18:54,319
who's going to be
our expert bobsled coach.

304
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:58,368
Sanka. Hit it, man.

305
00:18:58,436 --> 00:19:02,930
You're on the air, sled god.

306
00:19:03,007 --> 00:19:06,272
Gentlemen, a bobsled
is a simple thing.

307
00:19:06,343 --> 00:19:08,277
[Man]
Yeah, so's a toilet!

308
00:19:08,345 --> 00:19:10,905
[Crowd Laughing]

309
00:19:10,981 --> 00:19:14,974
Thank you. Thank you very much.
Basically, what you're looking to do...

310
00:19:15,052 --> 00:19:20,422
is get your sorry rear ends from the top
of an icy chute to the bottom.

311
00:19:20,491 --> 00:19:23,983
You're ziggin', you're zaggin'.

312
00:19:24,061 --> 00:19:28,088
It's the biggest, coldest
roller coaster you've ever been on.

313
00:19:29,834 --> 00:19:31,859
Ice.

314
00:19:33,637 --> 00:19:36,299
Oooh. Ooh.
[Chuckles]

315
00:19:36,373 --> 00:19:40,742
[Irv]
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

316
00:19:40,811 --> 00:19:43,712
I almost forgot, uh...

317
00:19:43,781 --> 00:19:46,944
One minor drawback
to this delightful winter sport...

318
00:19:47,017 --> 00:19:49,611
is the high-speed crash.

319
00:19:49,687 --> 00:19:51,951
That hurt. Ah.

320
00:19:52,022 --> 00:19:56,482
Always remember, your bones
will not break in a bobsled.

321
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:58,585
No, no. They shatter.

322
00:20:01,198 --> 00:20:03,666
Eee!

323
00:20:05,703 --> 00:20:09,537
So... who wants in?

324
00:20:23,988 --> 00:20:27,253
Look. Baldy's here.

325
00:20:27,324 --> 00:20:29,349
Glad you could make it, man.

326
00:20:29,426 --> 00:20:34,295
- Don't touch me!
- No problem.

327
00:20:34,365 --> 00:20:37,528
- So what's your name?
- Yul Brenner.

328
00:20:40,704 --> 00:20:44,196
Well, it's good to have you
as a teammate, Brenner.

329
00:20:44,275 --> 00:20:47,108
Let's get one thing straight,
Bannock.

330
00:20:47,177 --> 00:20:51,841
We may be on the same team,
but I am no one's teammate.

331
00:20:51,916 --> 00:20:54,510
- Long as you come here to bobsled...
- Hey, listen, man,

332
00:20:54,585 --> 00:20:56,815
the only reason why I come here...

333
00:20:56,887 --> 00:21:00,482
is to get off
of this stinkin' island.

334
00:21:00,558 --> 00:21:05,621
If I have to take one of those
bobsleds to do it, then all right.

335
00:21:05,696 --> 00:21:08,631
- No problem.
- [Irv] Ah, yes.

336
00:21:08,699 --> 00:21:12,396
Yes, I have a problem. There's
no such thing as a three-man sled.

337
00:21:12,469 --> 00:21:15,563
You're one Jamaican short.

338
00:21:15,639 --> 00:21:18,733
Hey.

339
00:21:18,809 --> 00:21:22,040
The meeting start yet?
Uh-oh.

340
00:21:22,112 --> 00:21:25,411
You! I'll kill you.

341
00:21:25,482 --> 00:21:27,609
- [Derice] Wait! Hold on!
- College boy, I'll kill you!

342
00:21:27,685 --> 00:21:30,313
[Sanka] Hey, think, man, think!
Easy! Whoa! Down, boy!

343
00:21:30,387 --> 00:21:33,220
[Men Shouting, Chair Clattering]

344
00:21:33,290 --> 00:21:36,726
Kill him
and we don't have a team.

345
00:21:36,794 --> 00:21:39,160
I'm not ridin'
in the same sled as that.

346
00:21:39,229 --> 00:21:42,198
He tripped me too, you know.
But in case you haven't noticed,

347
00:21:42,266 --> 00:21:44,666
there's no one else here.

348
00:21:44,735 --> 00:21:47,636
- You're crowdin' me, slinky head.
- [Chuckling]

349
00:21:47,705 --> 00:21:49,639
Slinky head.
That's a good one.

350
00:21:49,707 --> 00:21:52,175
- What are you laughing about?
- Nothing.

351
00:21:52,242 --> 00:21:56,645
If it wasn't for you, rich boy,
I'd be in the Olympics right now.

352
00:21:56,714 --> 00:21:59,308
I don't know what you all are arguing
about 'cause Derice was gonna...

353
00:21:59,383 --> 00:22:02,819
- Beat both of your butts anyway.
- What are you talkin' about?

354
00:22:02,886 --> 00:22:05,855
- How 'bout I beat your butt right now?
- How 'bout I draw a line...

355
00:22:05,923 --> 00:22:08,289
down the middle of your head
so it looks like a butt?

356
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:10,293
[Chuckling]

357
00:22:14,698 --> 00:22:16,996
Forget it, man, I'm gone.

358
00:22:17,067 --> 00:22:19,763
[Derice]
Fine. Stay here on the island.

359
00:22:19,837 --> 00:22:23,000
We're going to Canada.

360
00:22:26,510 --> 00:22:30,776
All right. I'll do it.

361
00:22:30,848 --> 00:22:34,648
But you better tell
this mama's boy...

362
00:22:34,718 --> 00:22:37,084
to stay the hell away from me.

363
00:22:37,154 --> 00:22:39,554
You understand?

364
00:22:39,623 --> 00:22:42,990
No problem.

365
00:22:43,060 --> 00:22:47,292
Hey, Irv.
Say hello to the first...

366
00:22:47,364 --> 00:22:50,060
Jamaican bobsled team.

367
00:22:56,807 --> 00:22:59,503
Oh, goody.

368
00:22:59,576 --> 00:23:03,945
Gentlemen,
this... is a bobsled.

369
00:23:04,014 --> 00:23:06,642
Sort of.

370
00:23:06,717 --> 00:23:10,118
- All right, here's what we're gonna do. Yul...
- Don't touch me.

371
00:23:10,187 --> 00:23:14,123
Of course. Sorry. You're
gonna be the second middleman.

372
00:23:14,191 --> 00:23:18,287
You're strong, you're fast
and you're gonna love that seat.

373
00:23:18,362 --> 00:23:20,421
Junior,
you're the first middleman.

374
00:23:20,497 --> 00:23:24,263
You're quick, you're sharp.
Hop in. Sanka.

375
00:23:24,334 --> 00:23:27,303
- I know. I'm the driver, right?
- No, you're the brakeman.

376
00:23:27,371 --> 00:23:31,740
- No, no, I'm the driver.
- No, you're not. You're the brakeman.

377
00:23:31,809 --> 00:23:35,142
- I'm the driver.
- You're not. You're the brakeman.

378
00:23:35,212 --> 00:23:37,180
You don't understand.
I am Sanka Coffie.

379
00:23:37,247 --> 00:23:39,841
I'm the best pushcart driver
in all of Jamaica.

380
00:23:39,917 --> 00:23:43,478
I must drive.
Do you dig where I'm coming from?

381
00:23:43,554 --> 00:23:45,488
- Yeah, I dig where you're coming from.
- Good.

382
00:23:45,556 --> 00:23:48,650
Now dig where I'm coming from.
I'm coming from two gold medals.

383
00:23:48,726 --> 00:23:52,218
I'm coming from nine world records
in both the two and four-man events.

384
00:23:52,296 --> 00:23:54,992
I'm coming from ten years
of intense competition...

385
00:23:55,065 --> 00:23:57,465
with the best athletes
in the world.

386
00:23:57,534 --> 00:23:59,764
That's a hell of a place
to be comin' from.

387
00:23:59,837 --> 00:24:03,398
You see, Sanka, the driver
has to work harder than anyone.

388
00:24:03,474 --> 00:24:06,034
He's the first to show up
and the last to leave.

389
00:24:06,110 --> 00:24:08,340
When his teammates
are all out drinkin' beer,

390
00:24:08,412 --> 00:24:11,210
he's up in his room
studying pictures of turns.

391
00:24:11,281 --> 00:24:15,911
You see, a driver must remain
focused 100% at all times.

392
00:24:15,986 --> 00:24:20,047
Not only is he responsible for knowing
every inch of every course he races,

393
00:24:20,124 --> 00:24:23,651
he's also responsible for the lives
of the other three people in his sled.

394
00:24:25,295 --> 00:24:27,763
Now, do you want
that responsibility?

395
00:24:27,831 --> 00:24:29,924
I say we make Derice
the driver.

396
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:33,436
So do l, Sanka. So do I.

397
00:24:33,504 --> 00:24:37,031
[Sighs]

398
00:24:38,208 --> 00:24:40,699
Oh. The back is nice.

399
00:24:40,778 --> 00:24:44,373
[Junior]
All right, Father, listen here.

400
00:24:44,448 --> 00:24:49,283
Ya see, I've made up my mind.
I am going to be a bobsledder.

401
00:24:49,353 --> 00:24:52,550
That's right. A bobsledder.

402
00:24:52,623 --> 00:24:55,786
- [Dog Barks, Whines]
- Oh, really?

403
00:24:55,859 --> 00:24:59,090
Well, I'm sorry
you feel that way.

404
00:24:59,163 --> 00:25:04,601
Fine. Cut off my allowance,
because you see, Father,

405
00:25:04,668 --> 00:25:09,071
a man has got to do
what a man has got to do.

406
00:25:11,809 --> 00:25:14,903
[Car Horn Honking]

407
00:25:19,483 --> 00:25:23,476
- Just who I want to see.
- M-M-Me?

408
00:25:23,554 --> 00:25:27,422
- You know where I just came from?
- W-Where?

409
00:25:27,491 --> 00:25:32,656
I got you a job.
With Webster, Webster and Cohen,

410
00:25:32,729 --> 00:25:35,095
the biggest brokerage house in Miami.

411
00:25:35,165 --> 00:25:37,759
Oh, right.
Webster, Webster and Cohen.

412
00:25:37,835 --> 00:25:41,828
[Chuckling] That's right.
And you start end of the month.

413
00:25:44,575 --> 00:25:47,271
- Yes, but I thought that I would...
- Look.

414
00:25:47,344 --> 00:25:51,303
We went along with
this track nonsense long enough.

415
00:25:51,381 --> 00:25:55,511
And we agreed that it's time
to get on with your real future.

416
00:25:55,586 --> 00:25:57,884
Right?

417
00:25:57,955 --> 00:26:00,856
- I know...
- Right?

418
00:26:00,924 --> 00:26:03,620
- Yes, sir.
- Good.

419
00:26:03,694 --> 00:26:06,720
[Chuckles]

420
00:26:06,797 --> 00:26:10,528
I'm gonna tell your mother.
[Chuckling]

421
00:26:20,410 --> 00:26:24,938
- I guess we sure told him.
- [Whining]

422
00:26:25,082 --> 00:26:29,212
Winning a bobsled race is about
one thing: the push start.

423
00:26:29,286 --> 00:26:33,985
Now I know you dainty little
track stars think you're fast.

424
00:26:34,057 --> 00:26:39,290
Well, heh, let's see how fast you are
when you push a 600-pound sled.

425
00:26:39,363 --> 00:26:43,800
Now a respectable start time
is 5.7 seconds.

426
00:26:43,867 --> 00:26:46,893
If you speed demons can't
whip off an even six-flat,

427
00:26:46,970 --> 00:26:49,768
then you have a better chance of
becoming a barbershop quartet.

428
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:51,933
[Groaning]

429
00:26:52,009 --> 00:26:54,204
Derice, come on! Hey!

430
00:26:54,278 --> 00:26:59,181
- Junior, get in. Never mind.
- Ow!

431
00:26:59,249 --> 00:27:01,410
- [Laughing]
- Come on, fellas, move it back. Let's go!

432
00:27:01,485 --> 00:27:06,252
' Here on this mountain top
oh-oh '

433
00:27:06,323 --> 00:27:08,917
- 14.3. No good.
- ' I've got some wild, wild life '

434
00:27:08,992 --> 00:27:12,155
- 13.5. 11.7.
- ' I've got some bills to pay, oh-oh '

435
00:27:12,229 --> 00:27:14,959
This is what it's all about.
This is where you win or lose the race.

436
00:27:15,032 --> 00:27:17,660
Right here in the push start.
This is where you're gonna practice,

437
00:27:17,734 --> 00:27:20,202
right here, right here in a Volkswagen,
you're gonna practice.

438
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:22,864
- [Yelling]
- No! Junior, quit falling down.

439
00:27:22,940 --> 00:27:26,398
Come on, hustle!
Catch up to them. There you go.

440
00:27:26,476 --> 00:27:29,411
Whoa. No! Do it again.

441
00:27:29,479 --> 00:27:33,848
[Sanka] Whoa, whoa. Stop, Derice!
Stop! Wait for me! Wait!

442
00:27:33,917 --> 00:27:36,750
I'm in! Stop!
Slow down!

443
00:27:36,820 --> 00:27:38,913
[Yelling, Crashing]

444
00:27:38,989 --> 00:27:42,049
Great. Very good.
Try it again.

445
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:47,321
If I've said it once,
I've said it 46 times:

446
00:27:47,397 --> 00:27:50,958
Cold weather endurance is vital
to building a successful sled team.

447
00:27:54,371 --> 00:27:56,839
Cold enough?
[Chuckling]

448
00:27:58,742 --> 00:28:03,338
One, two, three!

449
00:28:03,413 --> 00:28:06,780
[All]
Aaaah!

450
00:28:09,186 --> 00:28:11,950
- ' Wild, wild life '
- [Sanka] Go! Go! Go!

451
00:28:18,295 --> 00:28:21,162
- ' Here on this mountain top '
- [Sanka] Whoa! Slow down!

452
00:28:21,231 --> 00:28:23,722
- ' Oh-oh "
- [Derice] Sanka, hit the brakes, man!

453
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:26,325
- I can't! It's stuck!
- [Derice] Hold on!

454
00:28:26,403 --> 00:28:28,268
Look out!

455
00:28:28,338 --> 00:28:32,775
[Yelling]

456
00:28:37,748 --> 00:28:40,842
[Groaning]

457
00:28:40,917 --> 00:28:44,318
- [Indistinct Police Radio]
- [People Chattering]

458
00:28:44,388 --> 00:28:47,789
- Sanka, you dead?
- [Groaning]

459
00:28:47,858 --> 00:28:51,487
Yeah, man.

460
00:28:51,561 --> 00:28:55,793
[Man] What have you done to the
police unit? I should arrest you.

461
00:28:55,866 --> 00:28:59,267
- [Man #2] Who owns this thing?
- We do, sir.

462
00:28:59,336 --> 00:29:03,204
- And who are you?
- The Jamaican bobsled team, sir.

463
00:29:04,741 --> 00:29:07,835
- [Laughing]
- [Laughing]

464
00:29:07,911 --> 00:29:10,505
Don't give me that business.
I wasn't born yesterday.

465
00:29:10,580 --> 00:29:14,539
5.9! 5.9! You did it!
You did it! 5.9!

466
00:29:14,618 --> 00:29:18,577
We did it! We did it! 5.9!
Get outta the way! Get outta the way!

467
00:29:18,655 --> 00:29:20,680
5.9, guys! What?

468
00:29:20,757 --> 00:29:23,726
- Who are you?
- I'm their coach. You guys okay?

469
00:29:23,794 --> 00:29:26,592
- Yeah, man.
- [Irv] How's the sled?

470
00:29:26,663 --> 00:29:28,597
Sled's okay?
Well, it's in the wrong place.

471
00:29:28,665 --> 00:29:31,566
Get it back to the top of the hill!
Let's move it right now, you slackers!

472
00:29:31,635 --> 00:29:35,628
- Move it! Let's hustle!
Come on, you guys, move it!  - [Team Groaning]

473
00:29:35,705 --> 00:29:37,138
[Thunder Rumbling]

474
00:29:37,207 --> 00:29:40,472
[Irv] I'm not asking
for a winter sports program.

475
00:29:40,544 --> 00:29:45,072
All I need is a lousy 20 grand so I
can get us to the Olympics. That's all.

476
00:29:45,148 --> 00:29:48,049
[Coolidge] How in God's name
are you going to get to the Olympics?

477
00:29:48,118 --> 00:29:50,643
These boys have never even
seen a sled race before.

478
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:54,554
Mr. Coolidge, I have been looking
at sledders since I was 12 years old.

479
00:29:54,624 --> 00:29:56,468
If I say these kids can
make it to the Olympics,

480
00:29:56,469 --> 00:29:58,651
they can make it to the Olympics.

481
00:29:58,728 --> 00:30:02,220
Okay. Well, I'll
tell you what we'll do.

482
00:30:02,299 --> 00:30:04,597
Practice down here
with the boys a bit more,

483
00:30:04,668 --> 00:30:07,398
and when you're a little further along,
I'll come along and see you...

484
00:30:07,471 --> 00:30:11,908
- No! No, no!
- Now just a minute, Mr. Blitzer!

485
00:30:11,975 --> 00:30:14,466
This country enjoys
a fine athletic tradition.

486
00:30:14,544 --> 00:30:16,876
And if you think I'm gonna give you
the little money we have...

487
00:30:16,947 --> 00:30:20,474
so that you can parade us around
in front of the world like a freak show,

488
00:30:20,550 --> 00:30:22,848
you've got another thing coming.

489
00:30:22,919 --> 00:30:25,717
It's bad enough how you
embarrassed your own country.

490
00:30:25,789 --> 00:30:28,280
I'm certainly not gonna
allow you to embarrass ours.

491
00:30:30,794 --> 00:30:34,093
No go, kid.

492
00:30:34,164 --> 00:30:36,496
That's okay, coach.
We'll get the money.

493
00:30:36,566 --> 00:30:39,228
Do the words "give up"
mean anything to you?

494
00:30:39,302 --> 00:30:41,532
Not a thing.

495
00:30:41,605 --> 00:30:44,540
[Sanka] ' Some people say you know
they can't believe '

496
00:30:44,608 --> 00:30:46,974
' Jamaica
we have a bobsled team '

497
00:30:47,043 --> 00:30:49,773
' 'Nuff people say you know
they can't believe '

498
00:30:49,846 --> 00:30:52,610
' Jamaica
we have a bobsled team "

499
00:30:52,682 --> 00:30:57,210
Hi. I'm here to offer you
an opportunity of a lifetime.

500
00:30:57,287 --> 00:31:00,552
We're lookin' for a sponsor
for the first Jamaican bobsled team.

501
00:31:00,624 --> 00:31:04,560
[Laughing]

502
00:31:14,504 --> 00:31:17,337
[Crowd Chattering]

503
00:31:32,489 --> 00:31:34,116
[Crowd Cheering]

504
00:31:42,699 --> 00:31:45,634
[Crowd Chattering]

505
00:32:21,938 --> 00:32:25,237
- Oh!
- [Smacks Lips]

506
00:32:28,111 --> 00:32:31,512
' We have the one Derice
and the one Junior "

507
00:32:31,581 --> 00:32:35,210
I'll pay you a dollar to shut up.

508
00:32:38,388 --> 00:32:42,051
[Joy]
You got $9.52 from Yul Brenner.

509
00:32:42,125 --> 00:32:46,027
Thank you.
We got $184 from Derice and me.

510
00:32:46,096 --> 00:32:50,897
Sanka, how did your singing
on the street go?

511
00:32:50,967 --> 00:32:55,165
How did it go?
It went like this.

512
00:32:55,238 --> 00:32:57,536
' 'Nuff people say you know
they can't believe '

513
00:32:57,607 --> 00:32:59,768
- Sanka, we know.
- ' Jamaica, we have a bobsled team '

514
00:32:59,843 --> 00:33:01,401
- Sanka.
- ' We have the one Derice..."

515
00:33:01,478 --> 00:33:04,379
[All]
How much?

516
00:33:04,447 --> 00:33:07,746
- I made $1.16.
- [Irv] Oh, that's great.

517
00:33:07,817 --> 00:33:10,411
- We're only short about 19,000 bucks.
- [Beads Rattling]

518
00:33:10,487 --> 00:33:12,978
- Sorry I'm late, everybody.
- [Irv] No, really. That is terrific.

519
00:33:13,056 --> 00:33:17,459
You can unpack your suitcase,
Junior. We're not goin'.

520
00:33:17,527 --> 00:33:19,461
Hmm, that's too bad.

521
00:33:23,333 --> 00:33:26,393
- [Sanka Whistles]
- [Derice] Whoa. Where'd you get it, man?

522
00:33:26,469 --> 00:33:30,405
- I sold my car.
- [Inhales] Yes, man.

523
00:33:30,473 --> 00:33:32,907
- I am goin'!
- No, we're not.

524
00:33:32,976 --> 00:33:36,537
Look here, Junior, I appreciate
what you're trying to do here.

525
00:33:36,613 --> 00:33:39,548
But we can't accept this money.
It just wouldn't be proper.

526
00:33:39,616 --> 00:33:42,608
Aw, Derice, if I hadn't
tripped you fellas,

527
00:33:42,686 --> 00:33:45,280
we'd already been goin'
to the Olympics.

528
00:33:45,355 --> 00:33:48,415
I want you to have it.

529
00:33:53,029 --> 00:33:55,395
You mean you want us
to have it, right?

530
00:33:55,465 --> 00:33:57,592
Right. Us.

531
00:33:59,302 --> 00:34:02,465
Thanks a lot, Junior.
Thanks a whole heap, man.

532
00:34:02,539 --> 00:34:07,775
[Yul] Remember. This doesn't mean
that I like you. You understand?

533
00:34:07,843 --> 00:34:09,603
- [Joy] Be sure to thank your father for us...

534
00:34:09,679 --> 00:34:11,840
'cause Lord knows he didn't
have to let you sell that car.

535
00:34:11,915 --> 00:34:14,782
Well, uh, he doesn't know
I sold the car.

536
00:34:14,851 --> 00:34:16,785
Um...
[Clears Throat]

537
00:34:16,853 --> 00:34:19,447
He doesn't know I'm
on the team, actually.

538
00:34:19,522 --> 00:34:21,752
He thinks I'm off to Miami...

539
00:34:21,825 --> 00:34:24,020
and I loaned the car
to a friend to work for...

540
00:34:24,094 --> 00:34:28,087
Webster, Webster and Cohen,
some place like that.

541
00:34:28,164 --> 00:34:28,985
- [All Laughing]

542
00:34:28,986 --> 00:34:31,600
- ' Some people say you
know them can't believe '

543
00:34:31,668 --> 00:34:34,034
' Jamaica
we have a bobsled team '

544
00:34:34,104 --> 00:34:37,471
- ' We have the one Derice '
- ' And the one Junior '

545
00:34:37,540 --> 00:34:39,531
' Yu... Sanka '

546
00:34:39,609 --> 00:34:42,476
[Derice] ' The fastest of the fastest
of Jamaican sprinters '

547
00:34:42,545 --> 00:34:44,672
' Go to Olympics
Fight for Jamaica "

548
00:35:19,215 --> 00:35:24,676
[Man On P.A. Speaking French]

549
00:35:24,754 --> 00:35:28,190
[Man On P.A.]
Welcome to Calgary, Alberta, Canada.

550
00:35:28,258 --> 00:35:30,818
- Come on.
- Home of the 1988 Winter Olympic Games.

551
00:35:30,894 --> 00:35:34,694
- This is it.
- We hope you all enjoy your stay.

552
00:36:08,965 --> 00:36:11,433
Sanka, man,
what you smokin'?

553
00:36:11,501 --> 00:36:15,528
[Coughing]
I'm not smokin'. I'm breathin'.

554
00:36:15,605 --> 00:36:17,539
[Coughing]

555
00:36:17,607 --> 00:36:20,371
All right, fellas,
this is us. Let's go.

556
00:36:20,443 --> 00:36:22,377
[Yelling]

557
00:36:22,445 --> 00:36:25,278
What's the matter?
You guys cold?

558
00:36:25,348 --> 00:36:28,909
It's not so much the heat,
it's the humidity that'll kill ya.

559
00:37:02,118 --> 00:37:05,747
[People Chattering
In Foreign Languages]

560
00:37:05,822 --> 00:37:08,347
[P.A. Announcer Speaking
In Foreign Languages]

561
00:37:14,797 --> 00:37:17,288
Excuse me, do you know
where you register for bobsled?

562
00:37:17,367 --> 00:37:21,098
[Chattering, P.A. Continue]

563
00:37:23,172 --> 00:37:26,141
Do you know where
you register for bobsled?

564
00:37:30,413 --> 00:37:32,347
- See ya.
- I'll see ya around.

565
00:37:35,718 --> 00:37:39,119
Hey, Mike. Good to see ya
again, pal. Take care.

566
00:37:39,188 --> 00:37:42,624
- Ja? Okay, ja.
- All the best.

567
00:37:42,692 --> 00:37:45,661
- Can I help you?
- Yeah, I'd like to register for tryouts.

568
00:37:45,728 --> 00:37:48,663
- What country?
- [Clears Throat] Jamaica.

569
00:37:48,731 --> 00:37:52,030
- What country?
- Jamaica.

570
00:37:52,101 --> 00:37:55,366
- [Sighs]
- [Computer Beeps]

571
00:37:55,438 --> 00:37:59,807
Well, what do you know?
Jamaican bobsled team.

572
00:37:59,876 --> 00:38:03,073
Okay. Here it is.
It says here...

573
00:38:03,146 --> 00:38:05,876
your qualifying run will be held
on the evening of the tenth.

574
00:38:05,949 --> 00:38:09,009
Your judges will be Shindler,
Gremmer and Kroychzech.

575
00:38:09,085 --> 00:38:12,919
- I know Kroychzech. He's a good guy.
- Yeah. [Clears Throat]

576
00:38:12,989 --> 00:38:15,890
In order to qualify, you must
complete the course safely...

577
00:38:15,959 --> 00:38:18,427
in one-minute,
two-seconds flat or under.

578
00:38:18,494 --> 00:38:20,826
- Used to be a minute-five.
- Yeah.

579
00:38:20,897 --> 00:38:23,593
Times change.

580
00:38:29,005 --> 00:38:32,065
- Irv? Is that you?
- Roger, how ya doin'?

581
00:38:32,141 --> 00:38:36,168
Hello, Kurt.
Been a long time.

582
00:38:36,245 --> 00:38:41,046
Obviously not long enough.
Hello, Larry.

583
00:38:41,117 --> 00:38:45,554
Jesus Christ, Irv.
What the hell'd you do to yourself?

584
00:38:48,191 --> 00:38:50,682
- Don't worry about them, Irv.
- Roger, you gotta do me a favor.

585
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:53,422
- What?  - Please. You know that
revolving restaurant thing?

586
00:38:53,496 --> 00:38:55,794
- Yeah. Half an hour?
- Meet me there in half an hour. Yeah.

587
00:38:55,865 --> 00:38:57,799
- Please!
- [Man] Roger, come on!

588
00:38:57,867 --> 00:38:59,801
[Roger]
I'll try.

589
00:39:16,052 --> 00:39:19,920
- Thanks, Roger.
- Yeah, well. What's up, Irv?

590
00:39:19,989 --> 00:39:21,706
- How about a drink?
- No, I'm fine.

591
00:39:21,707 --> 00:39:23,516
What's so important it couldn't wait?

592
00:39:23,593 --> 00:39:25,720
- You want something to eat?
- No, I m fine. What's up?

593
00:39:25,795 --> 00:39:28,286
- A salad or something...
- Irv!

594
00:39:29,832 --> 00:39:31,424
I need a sled.

595
00:39:31,501 --> 00:39:34,061
You came all the way
to Calgary without a sled?

596
00:39:34,137 --> 00:39:37,470
I got $4,800.
I just need something competitive.

597
00:39:37,540 --> 00:39:39,474
[Laughs]
For five grand?

598
00:39:39,542 --> 00:39:41,908
- I know you got something lying around,
Roger.  - But, Irv...

599
00:39:41,978 --> 00:39:45,379
- Anything.
- You know I can't do that.

600
00:39:45,448 --> 00:39:48,178
Wait a minute, Roger.
Remember when you were desperate...

601
00:39:48,251 --> 00:39:51,186
to make that last slot
on the '68 Grenoble team,

602
00:39:51,254 --> 00:39:53,654
and you pleaded with me
to talk to Kurt?

603
00:39:53,723 --> 00:39:56,658
Did I say, "Sorry,
Roger, I can't do it"?

604
00:39:56,726 --> 00:40:01,891
Come on, don't make me beg.
Roger, it's me.

605
00:40:01,964 --> 00:40:04,933
All right. Maybe I can get you
one of our practice sleds.

606
00:40:05,001 --> 00:40:06,970
You're a saint. You know that? A SAINT!

607
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:08,664
You haven't changed a bit.
You're still a saint.

608
00:40:08,738 --> 00:40:11,400
Don't get all mushy on me.
Just tell me one thing.

609
00:40:11,474 --> 00:40:13,442
Is this whole thing a big joke?

610
00:40:13,509 --> 00:40:16,637
Or do you really expect
these Jamaicans to qualify?

611
00:40:16,713 --> 00:40:20,376
Not only are they gonna qualify,
they're gonna turn some heads doin' it.

612
00:40:20,450 --> 00:40:25,717
Listen, three of these guys
can run the hundred in under ten-flat.

613
00:40:25,788 --> 00:40:28,313
I don't care who you are,
that's lightning.

614
00:40:28,391 --> 00:40:31,690
Yeah. But can lightning run on ice?

615
00:40:50,646 --> 00:40:52,739
- No problem, man.
- [Chuckles]

616
00:40:56,686 --> 00:40:59,621
- God!
- [Grunting]

617
00:41:06,429 --> 00:41:10,195
Irv! These special shoes
aren't very effective.

618
00:41:20,643 --> 00:41:23,669
Grip with your toes.

619
00:41:23,746 --> 00:41:26,408
All right, you sugarcoated
track stars.

620
00:41:26,482 --> 00:41:30,111
Move out and let the ice-Rasta
show you how it's done.

621
00:41:30,186 --> 00:41:34,987
- Whoa! Ah!
- Yeah, like that. Yeah. Good.

622
00:41:35,057 --> 00:41:37,890
[Junior] Hey, fellas,
look at my progress.

623
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:40,451
Touchin' me!
[Grunts]

624
00:41:45,635 --> 00:41:47,569
[Buzzer Buzzing]

625
00:41:47,637 --> 00:41:51,539
All right, fellas, that's it.
Let's get off the ice before practice.

626
00:41:51,607 --> 00:41:55,099
- What practice?
- That practice.

627
00:41:55,178 --> 00:41:57,772
[Speaking Russian]

628
00:42:00,483 --> 00:42:04,920
- Whoa. Ah!
- Oh!

629
00:42:08,257 --> 00:42:10,521
[Grunting]

630
00:42:10,593 --> 00:42:13,994
That's right. Ah!

631
00:42:16,199 --> 00:42:18,133
Good team this year.

632
00:42:56,172 --> 00:43:01,007
Eins, zwei, drei.

633
00:43:01,077 --> 00:43:04,137
[Grunting]

634
00:44:14,150 --> 00:44:18,177
Nice. Bobsleds.

635
00:44:18,254 --> 00:44:22,782
Oh, my. You should see this on the hill.
It's like a miracle.

636
00:44:22,858 --> 00:44:25,622
- What's "schweiz"?
- No, man, Swiss.

637
00:44:25,695 --> 00:44:27,788
[Yul]
This is the real thing, man.

638
00:44:27,863 --> 00:44:32,732
Gentlemen. I'd like to introduce you
to the newest member of our team.

639
00:44:37,940 --> 00:44:40,875
[Irv] Uh, you won't believe
what I had to go through...

640
00:44:40,943 --> 00:44:43,969
to get us a sled
in such good shape.

641
00:44:44,046 --> 00:44:48,949
[Clears Throat] If we're gonna
make it into the Olympics,

642
00:44:49,018 --> 00:44:52,579
this is the boat
that's gonna take us there.

643
00:44:52,655 --> 00:44:55,715
Well, I'm told she's
actually quite fast.

644
00:44:55,791 --> 00:44:58,589
[Metal Clattering On Floor]

645
00:44:58,661 --> 00:45:03,291
- I, uh, know she's not much to look at,
but, uh...  - Shh!

646
00:45:03,366 --> 00:45:06,028
She's beautiful.

647
00:45:08,771 --> 00:45:12,002
[Speaking Russian]

648
00:45:17,446 --> 00:45:20,711
[P.A.] All coaches must sign teams in
before approaching bob run.

649
00:45:42,671 --> 00:45:46,573
- [Irv] Here we go.
- [Grunting]

650
00:45:46,642 --> 00:45:48,735
[Irv]
Let's go. Here we go.

651
00:45:50,846 --> 00:45:53,713
- Hold on.
- All right, come on.

652
00:45:53,783 --> 00:45:56,684
[Irv]
Grab ahold. Here we go.

653
00:46:14,670 --> 00:46:18,572
[Sanka]
Ah. This is good.

654
00:46:21,577 --> 00:46:23,909
[Irv]
This is it. Everybody climb in.

655
00:46:23,979 --> 00:46:26,345
Hold up.
I don't understand.

656
00:46:26,415 --> 00:46:29,543
- We're not gonna push start?
- No, we're gonna push start next time.

657
00:46:29,618 --> 00:46:31,382
For your first run,
I'm just gonna nudge you off.

658
00:46:31,383 --> 00:46:34,715
Okay, everybody in. Let's go,
let's go. Come on, come on.

659
00:46:37,460 --> 00:46:40,494
- [Yul] Don't touch me.
- Hey, baldy, get off my foot.

660
00:46:40,495 --> 00:46:41,629
- Don't touch me!
- Here we go. Come on.

661
00:46:41,697 --> 00:46:46,464
Hey, Blitzer. Why don't you put
some training wheels on that sled?

662
00:46:46,535 --> 00:46:50,403
- [Crowd Laughing]
- That's funny. Ha-ha. Very funny.

663
00:46:50,473 --> 00:46:52,744
- You want to kiss my egg?

664
00:46:52,745 --> 00:46:55,103
- I'm not kissin' no egg.

665
00:46:55,177 --> 00:46:57,611
- Suit yourself.
- [Irv] Listen up, fellas.

666
00:46:57,680 --> 00:47:00,740
- I don't want you to worry about
lookin' good out there.  - Ah, Blitzy.

667
00:47:00,816 --> 00:47:04,752
You're going to tuck them in too?

668
00:47:04,820 --> 00:47:07,755
Hey. Seemin' to you
like nobody likes us?

669
00:47:07,823 --> 00:47:12,089
We're different. People
always afraid of what's different.

670
00:47:12,161 --> 00:47:14,493
Hey, Jamaica!

671
00:47:14,563 --> 00:47:17,691
Watch out for number 12 turn.
It's scary, ja?

672
00:47:17,766 --> 00:47:19,199
Oooh!

673
00:47:19,268 --> 00:47:21,429
What's his problem?

674
00:47:21,504 --> 00:47:24,632
He's Josef Grool. He's one
of the best drivers in the world.

675
00:47:24,707 --> 00:47:27,574
Yeah, he's one of the biggest
assholes in the world too.

676
00:47:27,643 --> 00:47:31,704
Don't listen to him; you listen to me.
Derice, right here. You got it?

677
00:47:31,780 --> 00:47:35,910
Remember, keep your hands soft
and your mind clear.

678
00:47:35,985 --> 00:47:39,978
- High in, low out. What is it?
- High in, low out.

679
00:47:40,055 --> 00:47:43,081
All right, put your helmets on,
everybody. Let's go.

680
00:47:43,159 --> 00:47:45,184
Here we go, come on.
Helmets on.

681
00:47:47,730 --> 00:47:49,664
- Hey, coach?
- Yeah.

682
00:47:49,732 --> 00:47:51,927
I cannot get my helmet on.

683
00:47:52,001 --> 00:47:54,799
- Thanks, coach.
- That's what I'm here for.

684
00:47:54,870 --> 00:47:58,465
- Oh, coach? L-I gotta go. You know.
- Yeah?

685
00:47:58,541 --> 00:48:00,133
- Hold it.
- Hold it?

686
00:48:00,209 --> 00:48:01,954
- Hold it!
- Hold it?

687
00:48:01,955 --> 00:48:03,235
- Yeah, hold it!

688
00:48:03,312 --> 00:48:06,941
B-But, coach, l, I can't hold it.
We're not bobsledding yet.

689
00:48:07,016 --> 00:48:11,112
- Oh, yes, we are.
- Coach! Coach!

690
00:48:15,558 --> 00:48:18,186
Coach! Coach!

691
00:48:21,897 --> 00:48:24,559
[P.A.]
On the track.

692
00:48:28,103 --> 00:48:31,937
[Sanka]
Coach! Aaaaah!

693
00:48:34,743 --> 00:48:37,610
[Sanka]
Aaaaah!

694
00:48:37,680 --> 00:48:40,672
Slow down! Oh!
Slow down! Slow down!

695
00:48:40,749 --> 00:48:44,981
Oh, my God! Oh! Oh, Derice!
Oh, Derice! I hate you!

696
00:48:45,054 --> 00:48:49,821
I hate you!
I hate you! Ohhhh!

697
00:48:49,892 --> 00:48:53,521
[Sanka Yelling]

698
00:48:53,596 --> 00:48:58,192
[Crashing]

699
00:49:01,470 --> 00:49:04,667
[Derice]
Sanka, you dead?

700
00:49:04,740 --> 00:49:07,402
Yeah, man.

701
00:49:07,476 --> 00:49:11,537
Well, you can pee now.

702
00:49:11,614 --> 00:49:13,809
Erm...too late.

703
00:49:16,685 --> 00:49:18,376
This is embarrassing.

704
00:49:22,124 --> 00:49:23,557
[Coughing]

705
00:49:23,626 --> 00:49:27,027
[Yul] Man, shut down
that hot plate, fool.

706
00:49:27,096 --> 00:49:29,594
Those bananas are stinkin'
like a dead dog.

707
00:49:29,595 --> 00:49:31,624
Back off, back off, you eight ball!

708
00:49:31,625 --> 00:49:33,595
This is my mama's secret recipe.

709
00:49:33,669 --> 00:49:37,901
And I hope you don't mind keepin' quiet
while I catch up on my reading.

710
00:49:37,973 --> 00:49:41,101
What are you talkin' about, readin'?
This is a children's book.

711
00:49:41,176 --> 00:49:43,667
- Oh, is that so?
- Yes, that's so.

712
00:49:43,746 --> 00:49:47,182
If that's a children's book, that mean's
it's too advanced for the likes of you.

713
00:49:47,249 --> 00:49:51,184
What are you trying to say? That I'm
not smarter than a little child?

714
00:49:51,254 --> 00:49:55,612
No. What I am saying to you is that you
are the kind of club-totin'...

715
00:49:55,691 --> 00:49:58,251
raw meat-eatin',
me-Tarzan-you-Janein',

716
00:49:58,327 --> 00:50:00,125
big, bald bubblehead
that can only count to ten...

717
00:50:00,126 --> 00:50:03,221
if he's barefoot
or wearing sandals.

718
00:50:03,299 --> 00:50:05,563
Say whatever it is
that you want.

719
00:50:05,634 --> 00:50:09,764
Because you're just like
every other fool on the island.

720
00:50:11,440 --> 00:50:16,207
You're going nowhere, Sanka,
and you're thrilled to death about it.

721
00:50:17,546 --> 00:50:20,606
But you see me?
You see me?

722
00:50:20,683 --> 00:50:25,052
I'm different
'cause I know exactly...

723
00:50:25,120 --> 00:50:27,247
where I'm going.

724
00:50:27,323 --> 00:50:29,689
And after l, Yul Brenner,

725
00:50:29,758 --> 00:50:33,023
win the Olympics
and become famous,

726
00:50:33,095 --> 00:50:36,189
I'm gonna leave the island...

727
00:50:36,265 --> 00:50:40,634
and live right down there.

728
00:50:40,703 --> 00:50:44,139
[Laughing]

729
00:50:44,206 --> 00:50:46,140
What are you laughing about?

730
00:50:46,208 --> 00:50:49,268
- What are you laughing about?
- That's Buckingham Palace.

731
00:50:51,245 --> 00:50:54,406
You plan on livin' there,
you're gonna have to marry the Queen.

732
00:50:54,883 --> 00:50:58,011
Yul, that's where
the Queen of England lives.

733
00:51:02,958 --> 00:51:07,122
[Sanka] Face it, Yul Brenner.
You can start callin' yourself Madonna,

734
00:51:07,196 --> 00:51:09,623
but you're still gonna end
up in an outhouse shanty

735
00:51:09,624 --> 00:51:11,997
like every other dockworking nobody.

736
00:51:12,067 --> 00:51:14,074
- Says who?
- Says me, rich boy.

737
00:51:14,075 --> 00:51:15,594
What you know about it?

738
00:51:15,671 --> 00:51:18,697
Well, I know my father
started off in a one-room hut.

739
00:51:18,774 --> 00:51:21,265
Now, he lives in one of
the biggest homes in Kingston.

740
00:51:21,343 --> 00:51:23,256
- Well, he ain't your father.

741
00:51:23,257 --> 00:51:24,972
- He doesn't have to be.

742
00:51:25,947 --> 00:51:29,541
All he has to do is know what
he wants and work hard for it.

743
00:51:29,618 --> 00:51:32,985
And if he wants it bad enough,
he'll get it.

744
00:51:33,055 --> 00:51:37,014
Look, believe me, Sanka,

745
00:51:37,092 --> 00:51:40,858
the more Yul Brenners we got
makin' it in this world,

746
00:51:40,929 --> 00:51:43,159
the better off this world would be.

747
00:51:43,232 --> 00:51:47,191
Especially for Jamaicans.

748
00:52:02,017 --> 00:52:03,518
Go ahead, Yul Brenner.

749
00:52:04,219 --> 00:52:06,078
You go get your palace.

750
00:52:17,266 --> 00:52:19,666
[Yelling]

751
00:52:19,735 --> 00:52:21,726
Move, move!

752
00:52:21,804 --> 00:52:23,738
[P.A.]
On the track.

753
00:52:29,244 --> 00:52:31,940
What do you have in there, a baby?

754
00:52:35,617 --> 00:52:38,552
- I can't believe you're still cold, man.
- Cold?

755
00:52:38,620 --> 00:52:41,953
I'm freezin' my royal,
Rastafarian nay-nays off!

756
00:52:42,024 --> 00:52:44,390
All right, we're up.
Let's go, guys. This is it.

757
00:52:44,460 --> 00:52:46,394
Gimme that.

758
00:52:46,462 --> 00:52:49,431
Okay. Now this is
our first real push start...

759
00:52:49,498 --> 00:52:51,796
but don't worry about it, okay?

760
00:52:51,867 --> 00:52:54,392
l-lt's no different than what we
practiced. We've done it a hundred times.

761
00:52:54,470 --> 00:52:57,769
Derice, right here.
Okay, get your helmets on.

762
00:52:57,840 --> 00:52:59,774
- Coach.
- Okay, okay.

763
00:52:59,842 --> 00:53:02,276
- Thanks, coach.
- All right. Let's go, Derice. It's yours.

764
00:53:02,344 --> 00:53:05,438
- Ridiculous. What's he doing?
- [Irv] Ready!

765
00:53:05,514 --> 00:53:10,781
One, two, three.

766
00:53:10,853 --> 00:53:12,946
- [Yelling]
- Go, go, go, go!

767
00:53:13,021 --> 00:53:15,819
- [Derice] Hold on! Wait!
- Now!

768
00:53:15,891 --> 00:53:17,825
- Now! Now!
- Whoa! Look out!

769
00:53:17,893 --> 00:53:19,827
- Now.
- [Sanka Yelling]

770
00:53:42,351 --> 00:53:45,946
[Speaking German]

771
00:53:52,460 --> 00:53:54,290
Those guys are pretty good,
aren't they?

772
00:53:54,363 --> 00:53:56,791
Good? They're the best.

773
00:53:57,566 --> 00:53:59,977
So you guys been having a
little trouble out there, huh?

774
00:54:00,078 --> 00:54:01,730
Ah, we'll be fine.

775
00:54:01,803 --> 00:54:05,740
I sure hope so. It'd be a real
shame to waste all that talent.

776
00:54:06,308 --> 00:54:09,575
I'm not worried.
And we have a good coach.

777
00:54:09,745 --> 00:54:11,679
[Laughs]

778
00:54:11,747 --> 00:54:14,978
Kid, I hate to say it,
but you gotta wake up.

779
00:54:15,050 --> 00:54:17,245
Coach Blitzer's
what's killin' ya.

780
00:54:17,319 --> 00:54:20,686
He's been useless
since the day he was busted.

781
00:54:20,756 --> 00:54:24,317
- What you mean, "busted"?
- The '72 Games.

782
00:54:24,393 --> 00:54:26,953
The guy hid weights in the front
of the sled to make it go faster.

783
00:54:29,498 --> 00:54:33,161
So what?
It's no big deal.

784
00:54:33,235 --> 00:54:37,399
Having your gold medals taken away
for cheating is a big deal.

785
00:54:39,107 --> 00:54:42,008
Derice, let's go.
We've got a meeting.

786
00:54:53,789 --> 00:54:56,425
Givin' my kid
a few pointers, Larry?

787
00:54:57,793 --> 00:55:00,990
Your kid's gonna need
all the help he can get.

788
00:55:05,767 --> 00:55:07,701
Coach.

789
00:55:10,838 --> 00:55:12,363
[Knocking]

790
00:55:13,976 --> 00:55:15,332
Maid service, sir.

791
00:55:15,333 --> 00:55:16,638
Would you like your bed turned down?

792
00:55:16,712 --> 00:55:19,545
Mint? Perhaps I could
dust your head.

793
00:55:19,615 --> 00:55:23,915
Whatever's wrong with you...
is no little thing.

794
00:55:25,587 --> 00:55:29,546
Hurry up, man. I have a dead grandmother
that moves faster than you.

795
00:55:29,625 --> 00:55:32,719
- Wait, wait.
- [Knocking]

796
00:55:32,794 --> 00:55:36,230
What that fool want now?

797
00:55:36,298 --> 00:55:39,290
- What?
- Sorry.

798
00:55:46,441 --> 00:55:48,773
- What do you have there, man?
- A telegram.

799
00:55:48,844 --> 00:55:51,779
I know it's a telegram.
What's it say?

800
00:55:55,684 --> 00:55:58,152
From my father.

801
00:55:58,220 --> 00:56:02,919
He says I have to
come home right now.

802
00:56:02,991 --> 00:56:04,925
[Sighs]

803
00:56:11,733 --> 00:56:14,327
' Workin' '

804
00:56:14,403 --> 00:56:18,271
' Workin' from payday
to payday '

805
00:56:18,340 --> 00:56:22,800
' Every time payday comes
you know I'm down to my last '

806
00:56:24,446 --> 00:56:27,313
' Well, I'm dreamin' '

807
00:56:27,382 --> 00:56:30,613
' Dreamin' of you all day '

808
00:56:30,686 --> 00:56:36,352
' When the working's done we're
gonna love that night away '

809
00:56:37,926 --> 00:56:41,589
' 'Cause we're goin' nowhere
and we're gettin' there fast '

810
00:56:41,663 --> 00:56:43,961
' When we finally make it
we can both look back '

811
00:56:44,032 --> 00:56:46,432
' On these hard times '

812
00:56:46,501 --> 00:56:48,799
' Just for a laugh '

813
00:56:48,870 --> 00:56:51,134
- Hi.
- Howdy, partner.

814
00:56:51,206 --> 00:56:54,437
' 'Cause when you got love you
don't need too much money '

815
00:56:54,509 --> 00:56:57,307
' I'm in love with you
and don't you know, honey '

816
00:56:57,446 --> 00:57:00,711
' We're goin' nowhere '

817
00:57:00,782 --> 00:57:05,116
- ' And we're gettin' there fast '
- You've worked too hard and too long.

818
00:57:05,187 --> 00:57:08,247
And let me tell you
somethin' else, Junior Bevil.

819
00:57:08,323 --> 00:57:12,817
If it wasn't for you,
we wouldn't be here right now.

820
00:57:12,894 --> 00:57:15,556
Wait.
But you don't understand.

821
00:57:15,630 --> 00:57:17,757
He is really mad.

822
00:57:17,833 --> 00:57:20,301
I mean, you don't know him
like I do, you know.

823
00:57:20,368 --> 00:57:23,565
[Sighs] I think I better
just do what he wants...

824
00:57:23,638 --> 00:57:25,572
and go back home.

825
00:57:25,640 --> 00:57:30,236
And forget about your teammates?
Blood fire!

826
00:57:30,312 --> 00:57:34,180
The man, you act like he's
the king of the whole world.

827
00:57:34,249 --> 00:57:37,218
But what should I do?
What should I do?

828
00:57:37,285 --> 00:57:42,222
Hey, Jamaica! Keep it down.
You are not owning this place.

829
00:57:42,290 --> 00:57:44,884
Sorry, sir, sorry. I...

830
00:57:44,960 --> 00:57:47,588
I didn't mean to bother anyone.

831
00:57:47,662 --> 00:57:50,495
You have no business here,
Jamaica.

832
00:57:50,565 --> 00:57:54,399
You and your stupid friend,
playing like you are bobsledders, ja.

833
00:57:54,469 --> 00:57:57,700
Why don't you tourists go back
to where it is you came from...

834
00:57:57,773 --> 00:58:00,071
and leave the bobsledding
to the real men.

835
00:58:00,142 --> 00:58:03,407
Well, um, I'm a real man.

836
00:58:03,478 --> 00:58:06,379
You want to say something, Jamaica?
Come on out with it.

837
00:58:06,448 --> 00:58:10,111
' You know that money can't buy '

838
00:58:10,185 --> 00:58:12,278
' This feelin' '

839
00:58:12,354 --> 00:58:16,620
' That we're sharing tonight '

840
00:58:16,691 --> 00:58:20,286
' 'Cause we're goin' nowhere
and gettin' there fast "

841
00:58:20,362 --> 00:58:23,923
Come here, man.
Out. Right now!

842
00:58:29,004 --> 00:58:32,633
Now, look in the mirror
and tell me what you see.

843
00:58:32,707 --> 00:58:35,175
- I see Junior.
- You see Junior.

844
00:58:35,243 --> 00:58:37,177
Well, you wanna know
what I see?

845
00:58:37,245 --> 00:58:40,942
I see pride. I see power!

846
00:58:41,016 --> 00:58:45,783
I see a badass mother who don't
take no crap off nobody!

847
00:58:46,754 --> 00:58:49,254
- You really see all that?
- Yeah, man.

848
00:58:49,724 --> 00:58:52,090
But it's not about what I see.

849
00:58:52,160 --> 00:58:54,185
It's about what you see.

850
00:58:54,262 --> 00:58:58,289
Now look in this mirror
and tell me again what you see.

851
00:58:58,366 --> 00:59:02,666
[Clears Throat]
I see... [Sighing]

852
00:59:02,737 --> 00:59:06,229
- Pride!
- Pride! Right.

853
00:59:06,308 --> 00:59:08,742
- Power!
- Power.

854
00:59:08,810 --> 00:59:10,744
- And I see...
- A badass mother...

855
00:59:10,812 --> 00:59:13,246
- Who don't take no... -
- Who won't take no crap off of nobody!

856
00:59:13,315 --> 00:59:14,574
- Again!
- I see pride!

857
00:59:14,650 --> 00:59:16,571
-  Can't hear you!
- I see power!

858
00:59:16,572 --> 00:59:20,649
I see a badass mother who won't
take no crap off of nobody!

859
00:59:20,722 --> 00:59:22,656
- Once again! Junior!
- I see pride!

860
00:59:22,724 --> 00:59:27,627
I see power! I see a badass mother
who won't take no crap off of nobody!

861
00:59:27,696 --> 00:59:30,426
- That's right!
- That's right! Junior Bevil!

862
00:59:30,498 --> 00:59:32,591
Where ya... Where he going?

863
00:59:44,613 --> 00:59:48,379
Pride. Power. Pride.

864
00:59:48,450 --> 00:59:51,886
Now you listen to me, buddy.
I will not be talked to that way,

865
00:59:51,953 --> 00:59:56,151
so you better come up with
a damn good apology... or else.

866
00:59:56,224 --> 00:59:59,159
- Or else what?
- Ow!

867
00:59:59,227 --> 01:00:01,491
Eh, Jamaica?

868
01:00:01,563 --> 01:00:05,465
- Or else what?
- Whoa!

869
01:00:07,435 --> 01:00:10,836
Come on, Jamaica.
Say something.

870
01:00:16,444 --> 01:00:18,378
No problem, man.

871
01:00:18,446 --> 01:00:20,971
[People Screaming]

872
01:00:26,288 --> 01:00:28,313
[Men Grunting,
Glass Breaking]

873
01:00:38,300 --> 01:00:39,864
Excuse me, missy!

874
01:00:40,635 --> 01:00:42,695
Yippee-ki-yay! Woohoo!

875
01:00:43,772 --> 01:00:46,673
[Grunting Continues]

876
01:00:46,741 --> 01:00:50,006
[Sanka] Oh, come on, that hurt.
Let me go. Oh-oh.

877
01:00:50,078 --> 01:00:54,139
- [Snickering]
- I can't believe this.

878
01:00:54,215 --> 01:00:56,445
I just can't believe this.

879
01:00:56,518 --> 01:00:59,146
Didn't one of you have the sense
to know better? Go on, laugh.

880
01:00:59,220 --> 01:01:02,018
I wanna see who's laughing
when Irv gets here.

881
01:01:02,090 --> 01:01:04,024
Now, wait, wait.

882
01:01:04,092 --> 01:01:07,619
When that East German fellow
go out and push my teammate,

883
01:01:07,696 --> 01:01:11,029
and blood fire,
we have to fight back.

884
01:01:11,099 --> 01:01:13,624
You don't see the Swiss team
fightin', do you?

885
01:01:13,702 --> 01:01:17,468
You don't see the Swiss team
drinkin' and carryin' on and such.

886
01:01:17,539 --> 01:01:20,508
And you don't see the Swiss team
smilin' neither.

887
01:01:20,575 --> 01:01:24,443
In fact, if one of those Swiss boys
ever come across a pretty girl,

888
01:01:24,512 --> 01:01:27,413
he probably yell,
"Eins, zwei, drei,"

889
01:01:27,482 --> 01:01:31,111
and try to push her down some ice.
[Laughing]

890
01:01:32,854 --> 01:01:35,721
- What happened?
- Oh, I took care of the whole thing.

891
01:01:35,790 --> 01:01:37,883
I told the owner of the bar
these guys were...

892
01:01:37,959 --> 01:01:40,393
mentally disturbed, so he's
not gonna press any charges.

893
01:01:40,462 --> 01:01:42,692
All right,
sled god does it again.

894
01:01:42,764 --> 01:01:45,392
Just shut up, Sanka.

895
01:01:45,467 --> 01:01:47,401
Now maybe you haven't noticed,

896
01:01:47,469 --> 01:01:51,200
but we aren't exactly winning
any popularity contests here.

897
01:01:51,272 --> 01:01:56,209
They hate me, they hate you,
they hate us.

898
01:01:56,277 --> 01:01:58,802
Now, if we're even gonna
think about qualifying,

899
01:01:58,880 --> 01:02:03,146
we're each gonna have to sit down
and take a nice, deep look inside.

900
01:02:03,218 --> 01:02:05,743
I didn't come all this way
to get my butt whipped.

901
01:02:05,820 --> 01:02:07,115
As a matter of fact, now that I'm here,

902
01:02:07,116 --> 01:02:09,257
I thought I'd do
a little whipping of my own.

903
01:02:10,625 --> 01:02:12,660
Good night, gentlemen.

904
01:02:19,300 --> 01:02:23,236
- [Door Opening]
- [Clock Ticking]

905
01:02:31,613 --> 01:02:33,706
- [Alarm Ringing]
- Aaah!

906
01:02:34,682 --> 01:02:36,598
- Rise and shine.

907
01:02:36,799 --> 01:02:39,118
- It's butt-whipping time.

908
01:02:39,187 --> 01:02:44,250
" [Whistling]

909
01:02:44,325 --> 01:02:49,262
" ["Rise Above lt"
By Lock, Stock And Barrel]

910
01:02:52,534 --> 01:02:54,468
' Rise above it '

911
01:02:57,572 --> 01:02:59,767
' Rise above it '

912
01:02:59,841 --> 01:03:03,038
- Not bad. Pick it up though.
- " [Continues]

913
01:03:03,111 --> 01:03:04,945
Come on, come on, come on, come on!

914
01:03:04,946 --> 01:03:06,046
Now, now, now, now!

915
01:03:06,114 --> 01:03:08,048
' Just rise above it '

916
01:03:08,116 --> 01:03:10,914
' Come on then
Rise above it '

917
01:03:10,985 --> 01:03:14,887
- Good. That's it.  - ' Even though the road
seems very long and narrow '

918
01:03:14,956 --> 01:03:17,516
- Five more. Come on, five more.
- ' Baby need to sharpen his pin '

919
01:03:17,592 --> 01:03:21,551
- Push it, push it, come on.
That's it, that's it.  - ' Just like an arrow '

920
01:03:21,629 --> 01:03:23,563
- That's it. Good, good.
- ' Got-a no place to go '

921
01:03:23,631 --> 01:03:26,429
- Good. You're doin' fine. You got any more?
- ' Believe us baby '

922
01:03:26,501 --> 01:03:29,732
Come on, come on. Get in!

923
01:03:29,804 --> 01:03:32,068
Oh! Hey!
[Grunting]

924
01:03:34,142 --> 01:03:38,670
- ' You gotta learn to believe in yourself, yeah '
- [Grunting]

925
01:03:38,746 --> 01:03:42,648
' This, little man, is what you can
achieve if you work hard and sacrifice '

926
01:03:42,717 --> 01:03:45,914
- ' If you've got a problem '
- [Whistle Blows]

927
01:03:45,987 --> 01:03:48,080
- ' You've got to rise above it Yes you do '
- Go, go, go, go. That's it.

928
01:03:48,156 --> 01:03:50,818
- ' And when you face a challenge '
- Gotta grip with your toes!

929
01:03:50,892 --> 01:03:53,690
- ' You've got to rise above it It's so large '
- Go, go, go! Now, now!

930
01:03:53,761 --> 01:03:56,286
' If those storm clouds reappear
Oh, yes '

931
01:03:56,364 --> 01:04:00,232
- [Grunting Continues]
- ' You don't never have to fear. Just rise above it '

932
01:04:00,301 --> 01:04:03,099
' You, you've got to
rise above it '

933
01:04:03,171 --> 01:04:07,665
- [Grunting Continues]
- ' I tell ya once and I tell ya twice '

934
01:04:07,742 --> 01:04:11,200
You're gonna have to do this
on your own one day.

935
01:04:11,279 --> 01:04:14,976
' Come now, come now
and take my advice '

936
01:04:15,049 --> 01:04:17,040
' Rise above it '

937
01:04:17,118 --> 01:04:21,111
- [Grunts]
- ' Rise above it '

938
01:04:21,189 --> 01:04:24,852
[Irv] Go, go, go, go, go!
Now, now, now, now, now!

939
01:04:24,926 --> 01:04:26,860
- Straight. Right.
- Turn six.

940
01:04:26,928 --> 01:04:29,453
- Turn seven. Turn eight.
- Straight. Right.

941
01:04:29,531 --> 01:04:33,524
- ' Follow me, follow me, follow me follow me,
rise above it '  - That's it, that's it!

942
01:04:33,601 --> 01:04:36,263
' Rise above it '

943
01:04:36,337 --> 01:04:41,434
" [Singing In Jamaican]

944
01:04:41,509 --> 01:04:44,205
' Rise above it
You can do it '

945
01:04:44,279 --> 01:04:47,214
' Rise above it
You can do it "

946
01:04:49,817 --> 01:04:51,910
[Irv]
Okay, guys,

947
01:04:51,986 --> 01:04:54,682
tonight's the night.

948
01:04:56,424 --> 01:04:58,224
Now, in a few minutes,
you're gonna get a chance

949
01:04:58,225 --> 01:05:01,694
to do something that no one
in your country has ever done.

950
01:05:02,363 --> 01:05:03,994
I was gonna save this for the Olympics,

951
01:05:04,067 --> 01:05:09,827
but I figure if we're going to convince
these judges that we are world-class sledders,

952
01:05:10,705 --> 01:05:14,664
then we had better look
like world-class sledders.

953
01:05:15,743 --> 01:05:19,839
- Oh, man, yes.
- Oh, man. Nice.

954
01:05:25,653 --> 01:05:27,780
I freeze in this.

955
01:05:27,855 --> 01:05:31,222
[Grunting, Yelling]

956
01:05:33,561 --> 01:05:36,029
[P.A.]
On the track.

957
01:05:43,271 --> 01:05:45,535
Hello, gentlemen.

958
01:05:45,607 --> 01:05:49,099
Irv, this is Karl Shindler.
He'll be watching the middle track.

959
01:05:49,177 --> 01:05:51,077
How do you do?

960
01:05:51,145 --> 01:05:54,282
- And this is August Gremmer.
He'll be judging the push starts.

961
01:05:54,650 --> 01:05:58,915
- Hi.
- I'm your third official up in the tower.

962
01:05:58,987 --> 01:06:01,683
You? What happened
to Kroychzech?

963
01:06:01,756 --> 01:06:04,816
He came down sick this morning.
I'm taking his place.

964
01:06:05,792 --> 01:06:07,493
Oh, goody.

965
01:06:07,862 --> 01:06:11,298
Oh. The Alliance has decided
to change the qualifying time...

966
01:06:11,366 --> 01:06:13,834
from a minute-two
to a minute-flat.

967
01:06:13,901 --> 01:06:15,965
Is that clear?

968
01:06:17,938 --> 01:06:20,765
[Jamaican Accent]
No problem, man.

969
01:06:26,481 --> 01:06:29,348
Go get 'em, kid.

970
01:06:34,155 --> 01:06:36,281
[On Speaker]
Track is clear for Jamaica One.

971
01:06:46,834 --> 01:06:51,999
Eins... zwei... drei.

972
01:06:52,073 --> 01:06:55,702
[Grunting, Yelling]

973
01:06:55,777 --> 01:06:58,439
Go, go, go!
Now, now, now, now!

974
01:07:01,849 --> 01:07:05,080
- All right, what was that time?
- 6.13

975
01:07:46,294 --> 01:07:49,161
Under 60. Is it under 60?

976
01:08:00,775 --> 01:08:03,437
- [Cheering]
- Yes! Derice... Bannock!

977
01:08:03,511 --> 01:08:07,914
Whoo-hoo, 59 points!
[Laughing]

978
01:08:07,982 --> 01:08:12,919
Oh. I'm, uh, I'm sorry.
I'm outta here. That's terrific.

979
01:08:12,987 --> 01:08:16,286
- [Laughing Continues]
- [Cheering Continues]

980
01:08:16,357 --> 01:08:19,121
Derice!

981
01:08:19,193 --> 01:08:21,687
- " [Reggae]
- [Irv] Ah, it was great.

982
01:08:22,363 --> 01:08:24,660
[Derice] They couldn't beat us.
I know we were the best.

983
01:08:25,633 --> 01:08:28,932
[Irv]
...inspired you guys, that's all.

984
01:08:29,003 --> 01:08:32,563
Nobody had that much fun
in a sled since Santa Claus.

985
01:08:33,541 --> 01:08:36,339
Fellas, here's
to followin' your dreams.

986
01:08:36,411 --> 01:08:38,379
- Yeah, man.
- [Together] Followin' your dreams.

987
01:08:38,446 --> 01:08:41,779
I said it to your father the first time
I met him, and I'll say it again.

988
01:08:41,849 --> 01:08:45,910
- Sprinters make the best bobsledders.
- Here's to sprinting.

989
01:08:45,987 --> 01:08:49,047
So, what are we gonna
name the sled?

990
01:08:49,123 --> 01:08:52,092
How about "Tallulah"?

991
01:08:52,160 --> 01:08:54,560
- [Laughter]
- Tallulah.

992
01:08:54,629 --> 01:08:57,120
Tallulah.

993
01:08:57,198 --> 01:09:00,998
Sounds like a two-dollar hooker.
How you come up with that?

994
01:09:01,068 --> 01:09:05,698
Hey, you idiot,
that's my mother's name.

995
01:09:05,773 --> 01:09:07,798
- It's a pretty name.
- Tallulah. I like that.

996
01:09:07,875 --> 01:09:10,173
So, what's it gonna be, star?

997
01:09:10,244 --> 01:09:13,145
What are the people gonna be screamin'
when Jamaica takes the hill?

998
01:09:13,214 --> 01:09:17,446
I say we call it
"Cool runnings."

999
01:09:17,518 --> 01:09:19,486
- [Yul] Beautiful.
- I like it.

1000
01:09:19,554 --> 01:09:21,852
- It's very strong.
- Nice. Very nice.

1001
01:09:21,923 --> 01:09:24,790
Uh, what exactly does it mean?

1002
01:09:24,859 --> 01:09:28,260
"Cool runnings" means
"Peace be the journey."

1003
01:09:28,329 --> 01:09:30,263
[Together]
Peace be the journey.

1004
01:09:30,331 --> 01:09:33,664
- Cool runnings.
- [Together] Cool runnings.

1005
01:09:33,734 --> 01:09:37,397
- [Clears Throat] Excuse me.
- To the man in the orange suit!

1006
01:09:37,472 --> 01:09:40,839
[Laughing, Shouting]

1007
01:09:40,908 --> 01:09:44,366
- To the messenger!
- [Together] To the messenger.

1008
01:09:44,445 --> 01:09:47,107
[Laughing, Shouting Continue]

1009
01:09:47,181 --> 01:09:50,116
[Sighing]

1010
01:09:50,184 --> 01:09:54,746
We are officially...
disqualified.

1011
01:10:02,663 --> 01:10:06,531
- [Chattering, Laughing]
- Excuse me, gentlemen.

1012
01:10:06,601 --> 01:10:08,728
Kurt, I really
have to talk to you.

1013
01:10:08,803 --> 01:10:11,795
Excuse me, Irv.
I've nothing to say to you.

1014
01:10:11,873 --> 01:10:16,037
Yes, you do. I want to know
why you disqualified my guys.

1015
01:10:16,110 --> 01:10:18,900
As you were told, your team must
compete in an international race

1016
01:10:18,937 --> 01:10:20,206
in order to qualify for the Olympics.

1017
01:10:20,281 --> 01:10:24,684
But in an Olympic year, the qualifiers
count as an international race.

1018
01:10:24,752 --> 01:10:27,585
That may have been true
in past Olympic years,

1019
01:10:27,655 --> 01:10:31,113
but this year the Alliance
decided to change its policy.

1020
01:10:31,192 --> 01:10:34,161
Oh, please.
Change its policy?

1021
01:10:34,228 --> 01:10:36,950
The Alliance has the right to
do whatever they feel is in their...

1022
01:10:37,014 --> 01:10:38,358
...best interest of the sport.

1023
01:10:38,432 --> 01:10:42,766
We must also be concerned about
the potential for embarrassment.

1024
01:10:42,837 --> 01:10:44,771
Oh, forgive me.

1025
01:10:44,839 --> 01:10:48,707
I didn't realize that four black guys
in a bobsled could make you blush.

1026
01:10:48,776 --> 01:10:51,404
[Shindler]
I think we've heard enough.

1027
01:10:51,479 --> 01:10:54,710
Come on, Kurt. What you're doin'
is wrong and you know it.

1028
01:10:54,782 --> 01:10:58,912
Now, if this is about you and me,
then let's get it straight right now.

1029
01:10:58,986 --> 01:11:03,923
All right, 16 years ago,
I made the biggest mistake of my life.

1030
01:11:03,991 --> 01:11:07,757
I cheated. I was stupid.

1031
01:11:07,828 --> 01:11:11,195
I embarrassed myself,
my family,

1032
01:11:11,265 --> 01:11:14,928
my teammates, my country
and my coach.

1033
01:11:17,038 --> 01:11:20,064
If it's revenge you want,
take it.

1034
01:11:20,141 --> 01:11:23,133
Go ahead.
Disqualify me, banish me.

1035
01:11:23,210 --> 01:11:25,303
Do whatever you want,
but do it to me.

1036
01:11:25,379 --> 01:11:29,179
It was me who let you down, Kurt.
It wasn't my guys.

1037
01:11:29,250 --> 01:11:31,582
They've done everything
you've asked of them.

1038
01:11:31,652 --> 01:11:35,144
And they did it with all of you
laughing in their face.

1039
01:11:35,222 --> 01:11:39,682
Hell, it doesn't matter
if they come in first or 50th.

1040
01:11:39,760 --> 01:11:43,127
Those guys have earned the right
to represent their country.

1041
01:11:43,197 --> 01:11:46,792
They've earned the right
to march into that stadium...

1042
01:11:46,867 --> 01:11:48,801
and wave their nation's flag.

1043
01:11:48,869 --> 01:11:53,397
That's the single greatest honor
an athlete could ever have.

1044
01:11:55,343 --> 01:11:58,710
That's what the Olympics
are about.

1045
01:11:59,981 --> 01:12:03,644
Sixteen years ago,
I forgot that.

1046
01:12:03,718 --> 01:12:06,778
Don't you go and do the same.

1047
01:12:09,357 --> 01:12:12,417
[Sighing] I'm sorry
if I interrupted your meeting.

1048
01:12:21,035 --> 01:12:23,697
[Ringing]

1049
01:12:24,772 --> 01:12:28,469
Hello? Yes.

1050
01:12:30,945 --> 01:12:33,675
Yeah.

1051
01:12:35,082 --> 01:12:38,051
Right. Good-bye.

1052
01:12:41,355 --> 01:12:45,724
- What?
- Oh, it's the Alliance. God.

1053
01:12:45,793 --> 01:12:47,857
What did they say?

1054
01:12:48,629 --> 01:12:50,893
Aw, they said we're back in.

1055
01:12:50,965 --> 01:12:54,264
[Cheering]

1056
01:12:54,335 --> 01:12:56,496
Yes! Yes, yes!

1057
01:12:56,570 --> 01:12:59,198
[Cheering Continues]

1058
01:13:07,682 --> 01:13:10,446
[Man On Television] And a lot
is expected of the Italian team.

1059
01:13:10,518 --> 01:13:12,782
Did I miss it? Did I miss it?

1060
01:13:12,853 --> 01:13:15,879
No, child,
you didn't miss a thing.

1061
01:13:15,956 --> 01:13:18,584
[Broadcast Continues]... of Jamaica
made it all the way here to Calgary...

1062
01:13:18,659 --> 01:13:21,594
to compete in the bobsled event.

1063
01:13:21,662 --> 01:13:24,130
Their flag bearer is
the sled captain Derice Bannock.

1064
01:13:24,198 --> 01:13:27,133
Derice's father, Ben Bannock,
was a gold medalist in the 200 meters...

1065
01:13:27,201 --> 01:13:30,534
at the Summer Olympic Games
over 20 years ago.

1066
01:13:30,604 --> 01:13:33,835
And perhaps there's gold
in two generations of this family.

1067
01:13:33,908 --> 01:13:36,877
That's quite a story.
The Jamaican bobsled team.

1068
01:13:36,944 --> 01:13:40,539
It's a beautiful afternoon in Calgary,
and there is a lot more coming up.

1069
01:13:40,614 --> 01:13:44,675
So stay tuned for more exciting
coverage of the opening ceremonies...

1070
01:13:44,752 --> 01:13:48,745
of the 15th Winter Olympiad
from Calgary, Alberta, Canada.

1071
01:13:55,830 --> 01:14:00,164
Gentlemen, let's go check
into our new home. Come on, Junior.

1072
01:14:07,608 --> 01:14:10,042
[Irv]
Junior! Hey!

1073
01:14:14,548 --> 01:14:16,482
Junior!

1074
01:14:19,787 --> 01:14:22,446
Now, a lot of coaches
would be giving you one of those...

1075
01:14:22,522 --> 01:14:24,891
"Win one for the Gipper" speeches.

1076
01:14:24,959 --> 01:14:28,156
I'm not good at that stuff.
Instead, I thought I'd, uh,

1077
01:14:28,229 --> 01:14:30,857
lead you in a psalm of inspiration.

1078
01:14:30,931 --> 01:14:33,024
Let's bow our heads.

1079
01:14:33,100 --> 01:14:35,034
- Who's the "Gipper"?
- Shh.

1080
01:14:35,102 --> 01:14:40,039
Our Father who art in Calgary,
bobsled be Thy name.

1081
01:14:40,107 --> 01:14:42,940
Thy kingdom come,
gold medals won...

1082
01:14:43,010 --> 01:14:46,002
- [Giggling]
- On Earth as it is in turn seven.

1083
01:14:46,080 --> 01:14:48,571
With liberty and justice
for Jamaica and Haile Selassie.

1084
01:14:48,649 --> 01:14:51,117
- Amen.
- All right.

1085
01:14:51,185 --> 01:14:53,380
- Respect.
- [Knock At Door]

1086
01:14:53,454 --> 01:14:55,922
- All right.
- Jah Rastafari.

1087
01:14:55,990 --> 01:14:58,424
[Chattering]

1088
01:15:01,061 --> 01:15:03,996
[Chattering Continues]

1089
01:15:05,232 --> 01:15:07,166
Junior?

1090
01:15:12,506 --> 01:15:15,070
Now, you listen to me, boy.

1091
01:15:16,744 --> 01:15:19,144
You might not have done
what you were asked,

1092
01:15:19,213 --> 01:15:22,080
but you will do
what you're told.

1093
01:15:22,149 --> 01:15:25,209
- You're coming home.
- But, Father, you know I just want...

1094
01:15:25,286 --> 01:15:27,220
But nothing.

1095
01:15:27,288 --> 01:15:29,586
I didn't send you
to the finest school...

1096
01:15:29,657 --> 01:15:32,524
for you to go around
sliding on your backside.

1097
01:15:33,593 --> 01:15:36,529
- You must be mad.
- Yeah, but the team needs me.

1098
01:15:36,597 --> 01:15:40,192
- I don't want to hear any more about it.
- [Elevator Bell Rings]

1099
01:15:40,267 --> 01:15:43,202
Go and get your things.

1100
01:15:54,114 --> 01:15:56,480
I'll wait in the lobby.

1101
01:16:00,287 --> 01:16:04,383
- [Elevator Bell Rings]
- Pride. Power.

1102
01:16:07,928 --> 01:16:12,365
Father, when you look at me,
what do you see?

1103
01:16:12,433 --> 01:16:18,065
- I don't have time for games, Junior.
- Tell me what you see, please!

1104
01:16:18,138 --> 01:16:20,902
All right,
I'll tell you what I see.

1105
01:16:20,975 --> 01:16:22,909
I see a lost little boy...

1106
01:16:22,977 --> 01:16:25,912
who's lucky to have a father
who knows what's best for him.

1107
01:16:25,980 --> 01:16:27,413
[Elevator Bell Rings]

1108
01:16:27,481 --> 01:16:30,416
No, no, no, no, you don't know
what's best for me, Father.

1109
01:16:30,484 --> 01:16:34,318
I am not a lost little boy,
Father.

1110
01:16:34,388 --> 01:16:38,825
I am a man.
And I'm an Olympian.

1111
01:16:41,362 --> 01:16:44,092
I'm stayin' right here.

1112
01:16:46,533 --> 01:16:48,967
[Elevator Bell Rings]

1113
01:16:55,209 --> 01:16:57,439
Hey, Junior Bevil.

1114
01:16:57,511 --> 01:17:00,446
You're a badass mother.

1115
01:17:10,991 --> 01:17:14,154
[Chattering]

1116
01:17:16,664 --> 01:17:20,395
- Here, I got a couple.
- I like this one, yes.

1117
01:17:22,336 --> 01:17:25,897
[Foreign Languages]

1118
01:17:25,973 --> 01:17:29,374
Oh, Canada, indeed. This is Al Trautwig
along with John Morgan.

1119
01:17:29,443 --> 01:17:32,003
We're live at Olympic Park,
the brand-new bobsledding venue...

1120
01:17:32,079 --> 01:17:34,479
just a few miles outside
of downtown Calgary.

1121
01:17:34,548 --> 01:17:37,483
- Everybody, shut up. It's starting.
- ...extremely intense,

1122
01:17:37,551 --> 01:17:40,247
exciting competition
for the next three days.

1123
01:17:43,524 --> 01:17:46,118
[Chattering]

1124
01:17:48,896 --> 01:17:52,730
I am feeling very Olympic today.
How about you?

1125
01:17:55,502 --> 01:17:57,936
[Al Trautwig On TV] This sport, as we
well know, is made up of athletes...

1126
01:17:58,005 --> 01:18:00,769
who go to the edge and sometimes beyond,
and it is why we believe...

1127
01:18:00,841 --> 01:18:04,333
the next three days is going to be
extremely competitive and exciting.

1128
01:18:04,411 --> 01:18:08,211
And already, John, on day one, we're starting
things off with a gold medal favorite.

1129
01:18:08,282 --> 01:18:11,046
Well, the Swiss were fortunate enough
to draw number one in the competition.

1130
01:18:11,118 --> 01:18:13,416
We gotta make them the odds-on favorite
to win the gold.

1131
01:18:13,487 --> 01:18:16,684
But the East Germans, they're coming off
the gold medal win in 1984.

1132
01:18:16,757 --> 01:18:19,282
The Canadians, it's their home track.
You gotta favor them too.

1133
01:18:19,360 --> 01:18:22,557
And they've been doin'
very well in practice all week.

1134
01:18:23,731 --> 01:18:27,462
[Shouting In German]

1135
01:18:28,902 --> 01:18:31,769
- Eins, zwei, drei.
- Eins, zwei, drei.

1136
01:18:31,839 --> 01:18:34,740
- [Grunting]
- [Cheering]

1137
01:18:37,745 --> 01:18:41,374
One, two, three, go!

1138
01:18:49,823 --> 01:18:53,054
[Cheering Continues]

1139
01:18:53,127 --> 01:18:56,528
[Al Trautwig On TV]
Eighty miles an hour or close to it.

1140
01:18:56,597 --> 01:18:59,863
You know, Al, I'm looking at the times here,
and the course is gettin' extremely fast.

1141
01:18:59,900 --> 01:19:02,339
I was worried about the Austrian
team's safety in that last big

1142
01:19:02,340 --> 01:19:04,893
180 degree whiparound that draws
4 G's of Force from the athletes.

1143
01:19:04,972 --> 01:19:06,000
Well, if you were worried about them,

1144
01:19:06,001 --> 01:19:08,408
what are you thinking about
our last and next team?

1145
01:19:08,475 --> 01:19:11,842
Yes, it certainly seems strange that
surrounded by the ice and snow of Calgary,

1146
01:19:11,912 --> 01:19:15,905
we are about to watch a team
from the tiny island of Jamaica.

1147
01:19:15,983 --> 01:19:19,578
- [Cheering]
- Yeah, from Jamaica!

1148
01:19:19,653 --> 01:19:22,213
Quite a story for them to even get here.
They came out of nowhere.

1149
01:19:22,289 --> 01:19:24,348
And you know, there's a lot of teams
up here on top of the hill...

1150
01:19:24,425 --> 01:19:27,189
that sort of feel that Jamaicans
don't belong here.

1151
01:19:27,261 --> 01:19:30,059
[Booing]

1152
01:19:34,501 --> 01:19:37,993
- Hey! Hey! What are you doin'?
- Hey, what are you doin', man?

1153
01:19:38,072 --> 01:19:40,302
That's what the Swiss do
to psyche themselves up.

1154
01:19:40,374 --> 01:19:43,935
They also make them little pocket knives,
too, but I don't see you doin' that.

1155
01:19:44,011 --> 01:19:45,272
All right, guys, we're up. Come on.

1156
01:19:45,273 --> 01:19:47,640
Hey, knock it off. Knock it off, will ya?

1157
01:19:47,714 --> 01:19:50,911
Okay, let's go. Come on.
Get in your start positions.

1158
01:19:50,984 --> 01:19:55,114
We don't have to win the gold in the
first day. It's just like any other run.

1159
01:19:55,189 --> 01:19:58,158
Except this time,
100 million people watchin'.

1160
01:19:58,225 --> 01:20:01,251
[Irv] Derice, did you forget
something? Thank you.

1161
01:20:01,328 --> 01:20:03,262
- Ready.
- Ready.

1162
01:20:03,330 --> 01:20:04,991
- [Sanka] Ready.
- [Junior] Ready.

1163
01:20:05,065 --> 01:20:08,296
Eins... zwei...

1164
01:20:08,368 --> 01:20:10,666
drei.

1165
01:20:10,737 --> 01:20:14,036
Go! Go, go, go!
Go! Go!

1166
01:20:14,108 --> 01:20:17,839
- [Crowd Cheering, Indistinct P.A.]
- Get in! Get in!

1167
01:20:17,911 --> 01:20:21,608
[Al] The Jamaican team attempts
its first ever Winter Olympic event.

1168
01:20:21,682 --> 01:20:24,213
[Chuckling] And look at this.
They've got to get into that sled.

1169
01:20:24,316 --> 01:20:26,783
Now I've never seen anything like this.
I know it's not funny,

1170
01:20:26,784 --> 01:20:28,921
but how embarrassing.

1171
01:20:28,989 --> 01:20:31,822
Thank goodness. For a minute, I didn't
think they'd ever get all four of them in.

1172
01:20:31,892 --> 01:20:34,520
And that could have been
a disaster.

1173
01:20:34,595 --> 01:20:36,529
[Cheering, Shouting]

1174
01:20:36,597 --> 01:20:39,395
[John Morgan] Well, most importantly
here, when you do get in the sled,

1175
01:20:39,466 --> 01:20:42,333
you have to get in with catlike
movements; you need to get relaxed.

1176
01:20:42,402 --> 01:20:44,453
Look at the high line in Omega!
He bounces off the wall,

1177
01:20:44,454 --> 01:20:46,361
ricochets like a pinball.

1178
01:20:46,440 --> 01:20:49,967
The driver here, Derice Bannock, looks
like the sled's really drivin' him.

1179
01:20:50,043 --> 01:20:54,104
- That fool better watch his mouth.
- He better watch more than that.

1180
01:20:54,181 --> 01:20:56,183
This is the time when
this team may be thinking,

1181
01:20:56,184 --> 01:20:57,981
"This may not have
been such a great idea."

1182
01:20:58,051 --> 01:21:00,144
Their heads are bouncing around.
This is amazing.

1183
01:21:00,220 --> 01:21:02,984
Like rag dolls as they
come through the finish...

1184
01:21:03,056 --> 01:21:05,388
at a time of 58.04,

1185
01:21:05,459 --> 01:21:08,053
which will be good enough
for last place.

1186
01:21:10,797 --> 01:21:14,893
[Quiet Chattering]

1187
01:21:14,968 --> 01:21:19,530
You choked. It was yours
for the taking and you choked.

1188
01:21:19,606 --> 01:21:23,007
You were ready and you choked.

1189
01:21:23,076 --> 01:21:27,012
Well, maybe we should
go over the turns again?

1190
01:21:27,080 --> 01:21:29,417
You know the turns.

1191
01:21:29,418 --> 01:21:31,574
You know everything there
is to know about this sport.

1192
01:21:31,652 --> 01:21:33,586
I'll tell you something.

1193
01:21:33,654 --> 01:21:37,112
You had all better figure out
how to stay loose out there.

1194
01:21:37,191 --> 01:21:40,922
That's something
I can't help you with.

1195
01:21:40,994 --> 01:21:44,122
I'll see you tomorrow
on the hill.

1196
01:21:44,198 --> 01:21:47,759
[Door Opens, Closes]

1197
01:21:58,579 --> 01:21:59,795
- You know...

1198
01:21:59,796 --> 01:22:01,571
- when the Swiss want to get relaxed...
- [Groaning]

1199
01:22:01,648 --> 01:22:04,549
Oh, will you shut up
about the damn Swiss?

1200
01:22:04,618 --> 01:22:06,783
I mean, it was all that
"eins, zwei, drei" nonsense

1201
01:22:06,784 --> 01:22:08,782
that got us all nervous
in the first place.

1202
01:22:08,855 --> 01:22:12,154
Hey, man, look here. I'm just tryin'
to get us off on the right foot.

1203
01:22:12,226 --> 01:22:14,711
Well, the right foot for
us is not the Swiss foot.

1204
01:22:15,112 --> 01:22:15,992
I mean, come on, Derice.

1205
01:22:16,063 --> 01:22:19,555
We can't be copyin' nobody else's style.
We have our own style.

1206
01:22:19,633 --> 01:22:22,067
Kissin' an egg is no kind of style.

1207
01:22:22,135 --> 01:22:26,663
This is the Olympics here.
It's no stupid pushcart derby.

1208
01:22:30,477 --> 01:22:32,775
Let me tell ya somethin', Rasta.

1209
01:22:32,846 --> 01:22:35,838
I didn't come up here to forget
who I am and where I come from.

1210
01:22:35,916 --> 01:22:40,046
And neither did I.
I'm just tryin' to be the best I can be.

1211
01:22:40,120 --> 01:22:44,181
So am I. And the best
I can be is Jamaican.

1212
01:22:49,930 --> 01:22:51,522
Look.

1213
01:22:51,598 --> 01:22:55,398
Derice, I've known you since Julie
Jeffries asked to see your ding-a-ling.

1214
01:22:55,469 --> 01:22:58,131
And I'm tellin' you
as a friend...

1215
01:22:58,205 --> 01:23:01,140
if we look Jamaican,
walk Jamaican,

1216
01:23:01,208 --> 01:23:03,870
talk Jamaican and is Jamaican,

1217
01:23:03,944 --> 01:23:08,711
then we sure as hell
better bobsled Jamaican.

1218
01:23:08,882 --> 01:23:13,410
[Chattering, Shouting]

1219
01:23:15,489 --> 01:23:17,480
- [Derice] Greetings from Jamaica.
- " [Reggae]

1220
01:23:17,557 --> 01:23:19,991
' 'Nuff people say you know
they can't believe '

1221
01:23:20,060 --> 01:23:22,119
' Jamaica, we have a bobsled team '

1222
01:23:22,195 --> 01:23:24,755
' 'Nuff people say you know
they can't believe '

1223
01:23:24,831 --> 01:23:27,231
' Jamaica, we have a bobsled team '

1224
01:23:27,301 --> 01:23:29,462
' We have the one Derice
and the one Junior '

1225
01:23:29,536 --> 01:23:31,766
- Thank you.
- ' Yul Brenner and the man Sanka '

1226
01:23:31,838 --> 01:23:34,272
' The fastest of the fastest
of Jamaica's sprinters '

1227
01:23:34,341 --> 01:23:36,468
' Respect to the man
Irv Blitzer "

1228
01:23:36,543 --> 01:23:39,376
- All right, gentlemen, this is it.
- [Together] Respect.

1229
01:23:39,446 --> 01:23:41,380
- All right.
- Whoo, let's go!

1230
01:23:41,448 --> 01:23:45,042
[Al] We now come to the second chance
for the four intrepid men from Jamaica.

1231
01:23:45,118 --> 01:23:46,252
What do they have to do, John?

1232
01:23:46,320 --> 01:23:49,589
In reality, Al, I don't think the Jamaicans
have any chance of winning a medal.

1233
01:23:49,656 --> 01:23:52,147
Dear God, just let them
be better than yesterday.

1234
01:23:57,864 --> 01:23:59,456
- Ready?
- Ready.

1235
01:23:59,533 --> 01:24:02,434
Feel the rhythm, feel the rhyme,

1236
01:24:02,502 --> 01:24:05,767
get on up, it's bobsled time!

1237
01:24:05,839 --> 01:24:08,330
- Cool runnings!
- [Crowd Cheering]

1238
01:24:08,408 --> 01:24:12,606
[P.A.]
On the track.

1239
01:24:12,679 --> 01:24:14,423
[John] That's a hair
faster than the Swiss.

1240
01:24:14,424 --> 01:24:16,206
That's a real big
difference from yesterday.

1241
01:24:16,283 --> 01:24:17,821
[Al] This is an absolute
shock in the making.

1242
01:24:17,822 --> 01:24:20,447
Yesterday, they were
falling down at the start.

1243
01:24:20,520 --> 01:24:21,818
- Yes!
- Now they slide into place.

1244
01:24:21,889 --> 01:24:23,431
Yesterday, their heads
were bobbing everywhere.

1245
01:24:23,432 --> 01:24:25,414
Today they're almost in unison.

1246
01:24:39,373 --> 01:24:41,742
- [Al] Can this really be happening?
- What a difference!

1247
01:24:41,743 --> 01:24:44,224
Flying through the Omega,
looking posessed here.

1248
01:24:44,225 --> 01:24:45,742
It's not the same team we saw yesterday.

1249
01:24:45,812 --> 01:24:48,804
- Where did these guys come from?
- [Together] Jamaica!

1250
01:24:52,986 --> 01:24:56,080
[Cheering, Shouting]

1251
01:24:56,156 --> 01:24:59,216
Wow, 56.53!

1252
01:24:59,292 --> 01:25:02,921
Whoo! Yes! Yes!
Did you hear that time?

1253
01:25:02,996 --> 01:25:04,725
- Yeah.
- Yes! Ha-ha!

1254
01:25:06,299 --> 01:25:09,894
Whoo-hoo! Yes! Yes!
Come on, teammates.

1255
01:25:09,970 --> 01:25:13,406
- Jamaica!
- Yes! Yes!

1256
01:25:13,473 --> 01:25:14,527
- [Cheering]

1257
01:25:14,528 --> 01:25:15,742
- [John] That moves them
up into eighth place.

1258
01:25:15,810 --> 01:25:19,479
[Al] Watch out, world,
the Jamaicans are coming.

1259
01:25:36,696 --> 01:25:39,324
Derice, you in here?

1260
01:25:39,399 --> 01:25:41,765
Hey, coach.

1261
01:25:41,835 --> 01:25:44,565
Oh, there you are.
How're ya feelin'?

1262
01:25:44,638 --> 01:25:47,072
- All right.
- Good, good.

1263
01:25:47,140 --> 01:25:49,766
- You all set to follow
in your father's footsteps?

1264
01:25:49,767 --> 01:25:52,080
- I think so.
- You think so?

1265
01:25:53,281 --> 01:25:54,640
- All right, I know so.

1266
01:25:54,714 --> 01:25:56,206
That's more like it.

1267
01:25:56,207 --> 01:25:57,911
We're gonna go grab a bite to eat.
You wanna join us?

1268
01:25:58,484 --> 01:25:59,484
- Nah.

1269
01:25:59,585 --> 01:26:01,715
- I didn't think so. I'll
pick you somethin' up.

1270
01:26:01,788 --> 01:26:04,723
- Hey, coach.
- Yeah.

1271
01:26:04,791 --> 01:26:06,725
- I have to ask you a question.
- Sure.

1272
01:26:06,793 --> 01:26:10,456
But you don't have to answer
if you don't want to.

1273
01:26:10,530 --> 01:26:13,761
I mean, I want you to, but...

1274
01:26:13,834 --> 01:26:15,802
if you can't, I understand.

1275
01:26:15,869 --> 01:26:20,101
- You want to know why I cheated, right?
- Yes, I do.

1276
01:26:24,177 --> 01:26:26,645
That's a fair question.

1277
01:26:28,548 --> 01:26:31,142
It's quite simple, really.

1278
01:26:32,953 --> 01:26:36,218
I had to win.

1279
01:26:36,289 --> 01:26:41,090
You see, Derice,
I'd made winning my whole life.

1280
01:26:41,161 --> 01:26:43,493
And when you make winning your whole life,

1281
01:26:43,494 --> 01:26:45,825
you have to keep on winning.

1282
01:26:45,899 --> 01:26:49,164
No matter what.
You understand that?

1283
01:26:49,236 --> 01:26:52,501
No, I don't understand, coach.

1284
01:26:52,572 --> 01:26:56,030
You had two gold medals.
You had it all.

1285
01:26:58,144 --> 01:27:03,480
Derice... a gold medal
is a wonderful thing.

1286
01:27:05,719 --> 01:27:09,280
But if you're not enough
without it,

1287
01:27:09,356 --> 01:27:12,416
you'll never be enough with it.

1288
01:27:16,730 --> 01:27:19,198
Hey, coach...

1289
01:27:21,101 --> 01:27:23,160
how will I know if I'm enough?

1290
01:27:25,205 --> 01:27:28,504
When you cross that finish line,
you'll know.

1291
01:27:30,677 --> 01:27:34,841
[Door Opens, Closes]

1292
01:27:35,215 --> 01:27:37,577
Welcome back to the
bobsledding venue for this,

1293
01:27:37,580 --> 01:27:39,585
the last day of competition. It's medal time,

1294
01:27:39,653 --> 01:27:42,884
and John, the top six teams
are separated by only half a second.

1295
01:27:42,956 --> 01:27:46,687
- So it's very close.
- I didn't expect to see you here.

1296
01:27:46,760 --> 01:27:50,594
Well, my dear, we've got a team
in the Olympics, don't we?

1297
01:27:50,664 --> 01:27:53,030
The Jamaicans still have a chance
to win an Olympic medal.

1298
01:27:53,099 --> 01:27:56,728
Everybody shut up.
My boy's on TV.

1299
01:27:56,803 --> 01:27:59,271
And you're not the only one
to get excited about that.

1300
01:27:59,339 --> 01:28:02,206
I think the fans here have
an extreme case of Jamaican fever.

1301
01:28:02,275 --> 01:28:06,041
- Al, so do I.
- Oh, no, no, no, no. So do we.

1302
01:28:06,112 --> 01:28:08,444
Do I have to tell you
whose turn it is now?

1303
01:28:08,615 --> 01:28:11,675
- Jamaica to your start positions.
- [Together] Respect!

1304
01:28:16,656 --> 01:28:19,819
Hey, dreadlocks,
let me kiss your lucky egg.

1305
01:28:19,893 --> 01:28:21,827
[P.A.]
Next team up is Jamaica.

1306
01:28:21,895 --> 01:28:23,920
All right, fellas, that's us!
Let's go!

1307
01:28:23,997 --> 01:28:25,988
Here we go! Today's our day!
This is it!

1308
01:28:26,066 --> 01:28:28,899
Come on, guys, we can do it!

1309
01:28:28,969 --> 01:28:32,166
Derice...
see you at the finish line.

1310
01:28:32,238 --> 01:28:35,173
All right, it's all yours!
Let's go!

1311
01:28:35,241 --> 01:28:38,972
[Al] We might actually see
the Jamaicans win an Olympic medal.

1312
01:28:39,045 --> 01:28:42,173
So this is it.
We could see history in the making.

1313
01:28:42,248 --> 01:28:45,115
Feel the rhythm, feel the rhyme,

1314
01:28:45,185 --> 01:28:47,745
get on up, it's bobsled time.

1315
01:28:47,821 --> 01:28:51,313
- Cool runnings!
- [P.A.] On the track.

1316
01:28:51,391 --> 01:28:54,292
- [Cheering]
- Go! Go!

1317
01:28:54,361 --> 01:28:57,819
Go! Move! Go!
Move that bobsled! Go!

1318
01:28:57,897 --> 01:29:01,060
[Al] One, two, three, four,
all of them in, and look at them fly.

1319
01:29:01,134 --> 01:29:03,694
[John] Oh, man, they shaved another
couple hundredths off the start.

1320
01:29:03,770 --> 01:29:06,466
Al, they get better
every time down the track.

1321
01:29:06,539 --> 01:29:10,669
Go, Derice! Move!
Take that bobsled! Move!

1322
01:29:10,744 --> 01:29:15,180
[John] Look at the way the sled's coming
in and out of the corners. Very smooth.

1323
01:29:15,248 --> 01:29:16,634
It's like he's been driving
the sled for ten years.

1324
01:29:16,635 --> 01:29:18,479
Bannock looks really possessed here.

1325
01:29:18,551 --> 01:29:21,349
[Al]
Well, what the heck. Go, Jams!

1326
01:29:33,866 --> 01:29:36,267
[Al]
What a run Bannock is having.

1327
01:29:36,336 --> 01:29:39,466
He's letting loose
on this extremely fast course.

1328
01:29:41,041 --> 01:29:43,081
And even with that rickety old sled,

1329
01:29:43,082 --> 01:29:45,671
the Jamaicans are flying through the turns.

1330
01:29:47,947 --> 01:29:50,907
This does not look good.
Something's gotta be wrong.

1331
01:29:50,910 --> 01:29:54,644
The Jamaicans on a record pace as they
fly almost out of control around the turn.

1332
01:29:54,721 --> 01:29:57,155
- Move! Move that sled!
- Now the speed seems too much,

1333
01:29:57,223 --> 01:29:59,748
and I don't think he's going
to be able to hold it. Oh!

1334
01:30:53,680 --> 01:30:56,740
Derice, you dead?

1335
01:30:56,816 --> 01:31:00,843
No, man, I'm not dead.

1336
01:31:06,726 --> 01:31:09,559
We have to finish the race.

1337
01:31:26,479 --> 01:31:28,970
Excuse me, please.

1338
01:31:32,385 --> 01:31:34,444
Excuse me.

1339
01:32:39,452 --> 01:32:43,513
[Crowd Cheering]

1340
01:33:33,573 --> 01:33:37,839
Sehr gut, Jamaica. We'll see you
in four years, ja?

1341
01:33:37,911 --> 01:33:39,543
Yeah, man.

1342
01:33:42,882 --> 01:33:45,350
Junior Bevil.

1343
01:33:45,418 --> 01:33:49,718
- But it doesn't mean that I like you.
- We split.

1344
01:34:02,869 --> 01:34:06,270
- Thanks, Irv.
- Thank you.

1345
01:34:06,339 --> 01:34:09,775
- [Laughing]
- All right.

1346
01:34:09,842 --> 01:34:11,776
Coach, coach.

1347
01:34:11,844 --> 01:34:14,404
Hey, guys. I'm so proud of you guys.
You all right?

1348
01:34:14,480 --> 01:34:16,277
Gentlemen, can I get
a picture, please?

1349
01:34:46,520 --> 01:34:50,107
THE JAMAICAN BOBSLED TEAM RETURNED
TO THEIR COUNTRIES AS HEROES.

1350
01:34:50,316 --> 01:34:55,488
FOUR YEARS LATER, THEY RETURNED
TO THE OLYMPICS...AS EQUALS.

1351
01:34:57,623 --> 01:35:01,389
" ["I Can See Clearly Now"
By Jimmy Cliff]

1352
01:35:05,965 --> 01:35:08,525
' I can see clearly now '

1353
01:35:08,601 --> 01:35:11,536
' The rain is gone '

1354
01:35:14,040 --> 01:35:16,907
' I can see all obstacles '

1355
01:35:16,976 --> 01:35:19,877
' In my way '

1356
01:35:21,981 --> 01:35:24,643
' Gone are the dark clouds '

1357
01:35:24,717 --> 01:35:27,811
' That had me blind '

1358
01:35:27,887 --> 01:35:30,822
' It's gonna be a bright '

1359
01:35:30,890 --> 01:35:34,155
' Bright sunshiney day '

1360
01:35:35,928 --> 01:35:38,829
' It's gonna be a bright '

1361
01:35:38,898 --> 01:35:42,299
' Bright sunshiney day '

1362
01:35:46,005 --> 01:35:48,439
' Oh, yes, I can make it now '

1363
01:35:48,508 --> 01:35:50,976
' The pain is gone '

1364
01:35:54,013 --> 01:35:56,538
' All of the bad feelings '

1365
01:35:56,616 --> 01:35:59,176
' Have disappeared '

1366
01:36:02,055 --> 01:36:03,989
' Here is that rainbow '

1367
01:36:04,057 --> 01:36:07,925
' I've been praying for '

1368
01:36:07,994 --> 01:36:10,792
' It's gonna be a bright '

1369
01:36:10,863 --> 01:36:14,196
' Bright sunshiney day '

1370
01:36:17,970 --> 01:36:19,904
' Look all around '

1371
01:36:19,972 --> 01:36:24,341
' There's nothing but blue skies '

